ource_figures_not_digitized","id":"current_source_observation:0001","observation_end":"2011-12-19","observation_event_id":"toulon-2011-northern","observation_start":"2011-12-02","observation_type":"repeated_glider_transects_and_hf_radar_current_fields","physical_relation":"local_named_current_observation_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"Off Toulon, northwestern Mediterranean Sea","reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":null,"source_id":"source:361299ca16b625b2","source_locator":"Abstract; Sections 3.2, 3.4, 3.7 and 4; Figures 1–6","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/689/2018/","spatial_basis":"The source locates the study off Toulon in the northwestern Mediterranean and describes the repeated glider transects at 6.20°E. It does not provide a reusable digitized current footprint in this ledger.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_mediterranean_locality_to_osw_medi_semantic_state","state_boundary_limit":"The approximate OSW NECS polygon overlaps parts of the mapped Mediterranean coastal strip. The MEDI assignment follows the source's named sea, not a sampled footprint/polygon intersection.","state_id":"state:MEDI","time_detail":"Glider measurements ran 2–19 December 2011; HF radar fields ran 6–19 December 2011. This row records the combined study window, not continuous coverage by both instruments."},{"claim_id":"claim:current_source_observation:0002","entity_id":"current:canary","geometry_status":"source_reported_section_bounds_not_current_axis","id":"current_source_observation:0002","observation_end":"2009-11-11","observation_event_id":"orca-2009-canary-south-section","observation_start":"2009-10-15","observation_type":"hydrographic_section_and_inverse_box_model","physical_relation":"observed_local_cross_stream_section_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"ORCA 29°N section, 22.25–18.5°W","reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":[[-22.25,29],[-18.5,29]],"source_id":"source:5e15162e37e784c4","source_locator":"Abstract; section 6; 29°N ORCA section","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jgrc.20227","spatial_basis":"The paper reports the Canary Current extent along the 29°N section from 22.25°W to 18.5°W. This is a cross-stream band, not an along-current trace.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_section_intersects_approximate_osw_state_polygon","state_boundary_limit":"The reported cross-stream band intersects the approximate NAST E polygon; the state boundary and observed current extent are not surveyed together.","state_id":"state:NAST E","time_detail":"The dates bound the entire ORCA cruise; the exact occupation dates of this current band are not separately assigned here."},{"claim_id":"claim:current_source_observation:0003","entity_id":"current:canary","geometry_status":"source_reported_section_bounds_not_current_axis","id":"current_source_observation:0003","observation_end":"2009-11-11","observation_event_id":"orca-2009-canary-south-section","observation_start":"2009-10-15","observation_type":"hydrographic_section_and_inverse_box_model","physical_relation":"observed_local_cross_stream_section_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"ORCA 29°N section, 22.25–18.5°W","reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":[[-22.25,29],[-18.5,29]],"source_id":"source:5e15162e37e784c4","source_locator":"Abstract; section 6; 29°N ORCA section","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jgrc.20227","spatial_basis":"The paper reports the Canary Current extent along the 29°N section from 22.25°W to 18.5°W. This is a cross-stream band, not an along-current trace.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_section_intersects_approximate_osw_state_polygon","state_boundary_limit":"The reported cross-stream band intersects the approximate CNRY polygon; the state boundary and observed current extent are not surveyed together.","state_id":"state:CNRY","time_detail":"The dates bound the entire ORCA cruise; the exact occupation dates of this current band are not separately assigned here."},{"claim_id":"claim:current_source_observation:0004","entity_id":"current:portugal","geometry_status":"source_reported_section_bounds_not_current_axis","id":"current_source_observation:0004","observation_end":"2009-11-11","observation_event_id":"orca-2009-portugal-north-section","observation_start":"2009-10-15","observation_type":"hydrographic_section_and_inverse_box_model","physical_relation":"observed_local_cross_stream_section_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"ORCA 37°N section, 14.8–13.5°W","reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":[[-14.8,37],[-13.5,37]],"source_id":"source:5e15162e37e784c4","source_locator":"Portugal Current discussion; 37°N ORCA section","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jgrc.20227","spatial_basis":"The paper reports the Portugal Current between 14.8°W and 13.5°W along its 37°N section. This is a cross-stream band, not an along-current trace.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_section_intersects_approximate_osw_state_polygon","state_boundary_limit":"The reported cross-stream band intersects the approximate NAST E polygon; the state boundary and observed current extent are not surveyed together.","state_id":"state:NAST E","time_detail":"The dates bound the entire ORCA cruise; the exact occupation dates of this current band are not separately assigned here."},{"claim_id":"claim:current_source_observation:0005","entity_id":"current:azores","geometry_status":"source_reported_section_bounds_not_current_axis","id":"current_source_observation:0005","observation_end":"2009-11-01","observation_event_id":"orca-2009-azores-eastward-section","observation_start":"2009-10-26","observation_type":"hydrographic_and_ladcp_cross_stream_section","physical_relation":"observed_local_cross_stream_section_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"ORCA 24.5°W section, 33.5–34.5°N","reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":[[-24.5,33.5],[-24.5,34.5]],"source_id":"source:0567b05988a08497","source_locator":"Abstract; section 2, paragraph 6; 24.5°W ORCA section","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007129","spatial_basis":"The paper reports the Azores Current between 33.5°N and 34.5°N at 24.5°W. This is a cross-stream band, not an along-current trace.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_section_intersects_approximate_osw_state_polygon","state_boundary_limit":"The reported cross-stream band intersects the approximate NAST E polygon; the state boundary and observed current extent are not surveyed together.","state_id":"state:NAST E","time_detail":"The 17 stations of the wider 24.5°W section were occupied 26 October–1 November 2009; the exact occupation dates of this current band are not separately assigned here."},{"claim_id":"claim:current_source_observation:0006","entity_id":"current:azores-countercurrent","geometry_status":"source_reported_section_bounds_not_current_axis","id":"current_source_observation:0006","observation_end":"2009-11-01","observation_event_id":"orca-2009-azores-westward-section","observation_start":"2009-10-26","observation_type":"hydrographic_and_ladcp_cross_stream_section","physical_relation":"observed_local_cross_stream_section_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"ORCA 24.5°W section, 35.25–36.25°N","reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":[[-24.5,35.25],[-24.5,36.25]],"source_id":"source:0567b05988a08497","source_locator":"Abstract; section 2, paragraph 6; 24.5°W ORCA section","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007129","spatial_basis":"The paper reports the Azores Countercurrent between 35.25°N and 36.25°N at 24.5°W. This is a cross-stream band, not an along-current trace.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_section_intersects_approximate_osw_state_polygon","state_boundary_limit":"The reported cross-stream band intersects the approximate NAST E polygon; the state boundary and observed current extent are not surveyed together.","state_id":"state:NAST E","time_detail":"The 17 stations of the wider 24.5°W section were occupied 26 October–1 November 2009; the exact occupation dates of this current band are not separately assigned here."},{"claim_id":"claim:current_source_observation:0007","entity_id":"current:alaska-coastal-gulf","geometry_status":"source_reported_locality_no_digitized_section_geometry","id":"current_source_observation:0007","observation_end":"1989-07-15","observation_event_id":"shelikof-sea-valley-1989-alaska-coastal","observation_start":"1989-05-10","observation_type":"moored_current_meter_transport_section","physical_relation":"local_named_current_observation_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"Shelikof Sea Valley, Gulf of Alaska; not the exit-to-Shelikof-Strait mooring line","reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":null,"source_id":"source:48b84ff7f08f8e6e","source_locator":"Published article, PDF page 4 (printed page 26), Table 1 caption, 10 May-15 July 1989 sea-valley exception; PDF page 5 (printed page 27), section 2.2, mooring-array location in 1989; section 3.3 describes the coastal-current transport context. Published PDF: https://workspace.aoos.org/files/2656915/Stabeno_etal_2016_Longterm_Obs_ACC.pdf","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dsr2.2015.12.016","spatial_basis":"The paper identifies mooring arrays in Shelikof Sea Valley for the 1989 transport calculation. This is published local coastal-current evidence; no array endpoints, station coordinates, observed current axis, or footprint are digitized here.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_gulf_of_alaska_shelikof_locality_to_osw_alsk_semantic_state","state_boundary_limit":"ALSK is assigned by the source-reported northern Gulf of Alaska locality. This is a semantic regional association, not an observed-geometry intersection with the approximate OSW polygon; no BERS association follows from this observation.","state_id":"state:ALSK","time_detail":"Published Table 1 caption explicitly identifies 10 May-15 July 1989 as a sea-valley transport interval. The dates delimit this local calculation, not the full 1984-2014 study window or continuous coverage of the entire coastal system."},{"claim_id":"claim:current_source_observation:0008","entity_id":"current:kuroshio","geometry_status":"source_reported_instrument_points_not_current_axis_or_footprint","id":"current_source_observation:0008","observation_depth_note":"The source reports combined profiles spanning roughly 900 m, with the upper 50 m excluded; the downward ADCP at 123 degrees east malfunctioned. Deeper Luzon Undercurrent flow is distinct from the upper Kuroshio.","observation_end":"2020-05","observation_event_id":"luzon-18n-2018-2020-kuroshio","observation_start":"2018-01","observation_time_precision":"month","observation_type":"paired_upward_and_downward_adcp_moorings","physical_relation":"observed_local_instrument_points_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"Three moorings east of Luzon at 18 degrees north, 122.7, 123.0 and 123.3 degrees east","reported_observation_points_lon_lat":[[122.7,18],[123.0,18],[123.3,18]],"reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":null,"source_id":"source:4718092ead1ab8fd","source_locator":"Abstract; section 2 Data and method; section 3.1 Mean structure; Figures 1-3","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2025.1675413/full","spatial_basis":"OSW projects the three paper-reported instrument positions into the approximate coast-masked state polygons. All three positions fall in CHIN. These are mooring locations, not the Kuroshio axis or an interpolated cross-stream boundary.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_instrument_points_projected_into_approximate_osw_state_polygon","state_boundary_limit":"The CHIN link is a lookup of three instrument points against approximate display geography; it is not whole-current containment, intersection, or a measured state boundary. The paper places the current core west of the array.","state_id":"state:CHIN","time_detail":"The paper reports January 2018 to May 2020, without exact deployment and recovery days here. This is the reported study window, not a claim of continuous valid coverage at every depth or station."}],"named_eddy_footprint_candidates":[{"boundary_type":"figure_digitized_instantaneous_ssh_contour_proxy","claim_id":"claim:footprint_candidate:kraken:2013-05-29","coordinate_reference_status":"Longitude/latitude inferred from figure axes; source figure does not specify a geodetic datum. Decimal output precision does not imply survey accuracy.","embedded_figure_sha256":"b07f073dadda7d8bb8660184b43aa981a719d4944a647ac02bff84e28812015b","entity_id":"eddy:published:kraken-2013","geometry_id":"geometry:0158","geometry_sha256":"08d7c7f5d1234fc996b5b1ea2f049811fe5553c4f744fa88e6a8694df04c1c32","id":"footprint_candidate:kraken:2013-05-29","method":"Segment the single closed blue loop by three RGB thresholds; trace its outside pixel contour; linearly georeference from the manually read panel ticks; intersect the enclosed polygon with the coast-masked approximate OSW state shapes under 16 independent ±3-pixel axis-tick perturbations per threshold.","nominal_segmentation_case_index":1,"observation_date":"2013-05-29","physical_limit":"Dated 2-D instantaneous SSH contour proxy only. Axis-tick sensitivity can place part of this near-boundary contour in CARB, so whole-footprint CAMR containment is unresolved. This is not the material coherent-core curve, a 3-D ring volume, or a claim for August/October. Source JPEG quality, manual axis reading, line thickness, and schematic OSW state geometry limit precision.","review_