-north-slope"],"related_proposed_currents":[{"id":"alaskan-stream","name":"Alaskan Stream"},{"id":"aleutian-north-slope","name":"Aleutian North Slope Current"}],"source_locator":"Aleutian Current definition","source_url":"https://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/aleutian-current/","summary":"Aleutian/Subarctic eastward flow, westward Alaskan Stream and Bering-side Aleutian North Slope flow are distinct. The roughly 20 km North Slope width is not an Aleutian width. Western SST-front search bounds do not define a current axis, endpoints or paired width edges. Whole-current dimensions remain unresolved.","supporting_sources":[{"access":"Relevant HTML sections/captions read; figures and fields not digitized.","label":"Bering Sea circulation and separate North Slope identity","locator":"Mean Upper Ocean Circulation subsections.","url":"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/stab1878/stab1878.shtml"},{"access":"Relevant repository PDF text read; gradient front and search window are not velocity boundaries.","label":"Western Subarctic front and Isoguchi jets","locator":"Introduction, first Results subsection, Figure 1 caption; Methods Data.","url":"https://eprints.lib.hokudai.ac.jp/repo/huscap/all/70589/naturecommunications9_1190.pdf"}]}],"season_url":"seasons.html?current=aleutian","section_fingerprints":{"claims":"4e7a6b15ade387a415cf4e1ee70f2148069948498fbb98b910ed07490d8156f3","identity":"e101f21fd97cd88ddc12f86338a97a5143f843a453c5240c581080067d6424dd","measurements":"65e2e46fc1e56ae9ff8c05eed7801de668cfcad1b097c02bb928b5bdb00f33b3","media":"06cdbfeb1921d5de8713cf092bac7abca69706b3098a038125591ae9e7d30610","routes_geometry":"8e7068caec00e6d65e1743263fd4ed2198b4cbeea72568d919d5d7ce0080cb62","sources":"624a24bac9028601ba2e6035ae3f3c44fb27e321791de1e7628c85c2b9d86611","time_evidence":"4133c099f3ecfe1d6ac3c25c948d9fe3f981b46cb363642ddb2e940678d84a29"},"series":[{"diagnostic_url":"../research/aleutian-160w-2013-monthly-component-spans.json","evidence_role":"monthly_local_compone