phic current reduced to 20% of its maximum; geostrophic reference is surface pressure.","calendar_months":null,"canonical_current_id":null,"canonical_transfer_eligible":false,"extraction_method":"Transcribed published numerical widths after original-page visual review; no field or edge-coordinate digitization.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"geographic_scope":"Gimsøy hydrographic section near the Lofoten Escarpment; source-defined Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current, not Norwegian Coastal Current.","id":"norwegian-fer-2020-gimsoy-relative-geostrophic-span","is_confidence_interval":false,"layer":"Depth-integrated relative geostrophic current. Exact vertical integration limits for the width paragraph are unspecified; nearby mooring/transport layers are not assigned to width.","measurement_type":"published_campaign_relative_geostrophic_span","name":"Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current","observed_period":null,"original_regional_context":{"audit_file":"research/norwegian-fer-2020-gimsoy-width-scope-audit.json","audit_pointer":"/measurements/0","audit_sha256":"084f2ab755c06589ab5985e362621e44eb1f08ec684d74e1086b65ede3c8c8bb","catalogue_identity_ambiguity_retained":true,"comparison_figure":"figures/norwegian-fer-2020-section-width.svg","description_kind":"gimsoy_relative_geostrophic_span","display_aria_label":"Source-defined Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current at Gimsøy: reported 25 to 30 km relative-geostrophic span, no midpoint or annual extrema. Catalog naming ambiguity retained.","display_caption":"Gimsøy: author-reported 25–30 km span at 20% of peak depth-integrated relative geostrophic current. Four occupations, not four dated numerical widths.","display_method_note":"Surface-pressure reference; width integration limits unspecified. The 20.1 km effective mooring integration width and its 4 km assumed error are separate. Norwegian Current naming remains unresolved.","effective_transport_error_is_width_uncertainty":false,"effective_transport_