ce-scoped extent route","scenario_count":243,"scenario_range_km":[3900,4900],"scope":"Source-scoped named-current extent from first clear evidence near 16 degrees E to loss of a recognizable jet between 66 and 70 degrees E. Does not include the subsequent South Indian Ocean Current or northern leakage branches.","source_locator":"Printed p. 125, Section 3 paragraph before Figure 8: first clear evidence near 16 degrees E, meander near 25 degrees E, current progressively indistinct after 66 degrees E and absent in recognizable form by 70 degrees E. Printed p. 136, Conclusions: overall southward progression from 39 degrees 30 minutes S to 44 degrees 30 minutes S and separate naming downstream.","source_url":"https://www.cfoo.co.za/seaatlas/papers/agulhas_return_current.pdf","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":4500,"candidate_file":"research/atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"1256ace4b349ed71d251f4f30f4a7296a7b137641d855c795538b05d41337974","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","current_id":"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","figure":"figures/atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate","name":"Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["ETRA","GUIN","WTRA"],"ordering_sensitivity":null,"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_4","remaining_gates":["Review 35 W and pre-island truncation; source retroflections and eastern branches are not represented.","Obtain compatible depth/time-resolved velocity axis before physical length or seasonal dimensions.","Resolve island interaction and return-flow topology without treating generated eddies as named identities.","No occupied footprint, route-buffer width or whole-basin system length