tion uses Lass et al. (2000), Introduction: cold northward shelf-edge current and Angola–Benguela confluence near 15 degrees S; observed front at 16.5 degrees S in the April–May 1997 survey.","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Lass, Schmidt, Mohrholz and Nausch (2000), Hydrographic and Current Measurements in the Area of the Angola–Benguela Front, Journal of Physical Oceanography 30, 2589–2609.","locator":"Introduction (northward shelf-edge flow and confluence near 15 degrees S); abstract (front observed at 16.5 degrees S during April–May 1997).","role":"Source-specific northern branch/front convention; not an entire-current survey.","url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/abstract/journals/phoc/30/10/1520-0485_2000_030_2589_hacmit_2.0.co_2.xml"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":2200,"candidate_file":"research/north-brazil-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"250d6b1f2c4a497dcf6461ef545536b176f01b677eb5f85acdc008cb60706257","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","current_id":"north-brazil","figure":"figures/north-brazil-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"north-brazil-reference-path-candidate","name":"North Brazil Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["GUIA","WTRA"],"ordering_sensitivity":{"envelope_position_bounds":[6,19],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison.","overlapping_candidate_ids":["leeuwin-reference-path-candidate","caribbean-reference-path-candidate","east-greenland-reference-path-candidate","benguela-reference-path-candidate","black-sea-rim-reference-path-candidate","east-australian-reference-path-candidate","labrador-reference-path-