 2: source-water convention, coastal route and complex Tromsoflaket pathways converging near Ingoy; data section distinguishes local measurements.","role":"Ingoy gate context and continuity caveat; no drifter trajectory or velocity field digitized.","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011JC006996"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":2100,"candidate_file":"research/south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"7f6258f70942eead02f9c621b13b32db7effb641901e4933b50cbb51338647f2","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","current_id":"south-atlantic","figure":"figures/south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate","name":"South Atlantic Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["BRAZ","SATL"],"ordering_sensitivity":null,"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_5","remaining_gates":["Validate source anchor interpretation, depth and regional naming independently; the farthest observed float reach is not a whole-current endpoint.","Acquire dated float or suitable velocity geometry before measuring physical meander length; do not transfer this reach to the surface current.","Resolve eastern-basin continuation, SAC/ACC exchange and recirculation before a full-current length.","Keep all annual dimensions and physical width unresolved; complete canonical measurement and publication review separately."],"route_extent_kind":"western intermediate SAC reach","scenario_count":81,"scenario_range_km":[2000,2300],"scope":"Declared western intermediate-depth SAC reference reach from a 40 W, 39 S current-center context gate to the 16 W, 43 S Mid-Atlantic Ridge float-reach context gate. Excludes upstream Brazil/Falkland confluence paths, unresolved eastern-basin continuation and recirculation. Not a complete current or a digitized float trajectory.","source_locator":"Section 3.5, journal pp. 381–383 / PDF pp. 27–29: current center near 40 W, 39 S; easternmost RAFOS reach near 43 S, 16 W; large meanders and possible SAC/ACC exchange. Figure 11 is context only, not digitized.","source_url":"https://www.aoml.noaa.gov/phod/docs/boebel_et_al1999a.pdf","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":2000,"candidate_file":"research/agulhas-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"2b5a04d3b3a21029c61ffb96001080746ae8667be6eff3a1cabf59e56c1b2acc","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","current_id":"agulhas","figure":"figures/agulhas-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"agulhas-reference-path-candidate","name":"Agulhas Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["EAFR","SSTC"],"ordering_sensitivity":{"envelope_position_bounds":[9,19],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison.","overlapping_candidate_ids":["benguela-reference-path-candidate","north-brazil-reference-path-candidate","black-sea-rim-reference-path-candidate","east-australian-reference-path-candidate","labrador-reference-path-candidate","norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate","hiri-reference-path-candidate","canary-reference-path-candidate","somali-winter-reference-path-candidate","portugal-reference-path-candidate"]},"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_D_5","remaining_gates":["Independent review of regional extent versus coastal-jet naming and the retroflection/return handoff.","Validate offshore waypoints against reproducible bathymetric or velocity geometry; extend endpoint scenarios if warranted.","Canonical geometry/measurement integration and publication review before admission."],"route_extent_kind":"regional extent to retroflection","scenario_count":81,"scenario_range_km":[1800,2200],"scope":"Regional southward Agulhas reference route from 27 degrees S to a 40 degrees S retroflection gate near 19 degrees E. Includes an editorial approach to the turning region; stops before the eastward Agulhas Return Current. Excludes upstream Mozambique/East Madagascar branches, leakage and ring trajectories. This is a regional extent convention, not the narrower coastal-jet definition or whole Agulhas system.","source_locator":"Regional and Shelf-Scale / The Agulhas Current System: regional 27–40 degrees S description, retroflection at 18–20 degrees E and eastward return-current distinction; broader/early retroflections discussed separately.","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.837906/full","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":1900,"candidate_file":"research/hiri-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"a419f982ad804b3e06d96723819a14798a8fb6231f771d5e3144e1db30069a35","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","current_id":"hiri-current","figure":"figures/hiri-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"hiri-reference-path-candidate","name":"Hiri Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["ARCH","AUSE"],"ordering_sensitivity":{"envelope_position_bounds":[6,16],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison.","overlapping_candidate_ids":["leeuwin-reference-path-candidate","caribbean-reference-path-candidate","east-greenland-reference-path-candidate","benguela-reference-path-candidate","north-brazil-reference-path-candidate","black-sea-rim-reference-path-candidate","east-australian-reference-path-candidate","labrador-reference-path-candidate","norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate","agulhas-reference-path-candidate"]},"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_G_4","remaining_gates":["Scientific review of naming limits, layer and regional gate conventions.","Verify bathymetric and velocity correspondence; coarse land clearance does not establish a current axis.","Canonical admission and publication review; retain regional scope and editorial provenance."],"route_extent_kind":"broad Hiri regional route","scenario_count":54,"scenario_range_km":[1900,2500],"scope":"Broad Hiri naming convention: northward Australian boundary branch from an OSW 15 S bifurcation approach, clockwise around the Gulf of Papua entrance, to an OSW eastern Louisiade approach. Excludes closed gyre return circuits, direct mid-basin Solomon inflow, EAC, downstream New Guinea currents and eddy excursions. Narrower literature uses Hiri only south of PNG and proposes Gulf of Papua Current for the connected boundary system; no alias merge or complete system extent admitted.","source_locator":"Section 1 and section 3.1.5: northward branch initiated near 15 S, clockwise Gulf of Papua circulation and depth dependence. Figure 1 separates upper 0-300 m and deeper modeled flows.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2017JC013221","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Burrage (1993), Coral Sea Currents, Corella 17(5), 135-145.","locator":"Introduction, printed pp. 136-137: northward branch around Gulf entrance, exit around Louisiades and broad Hiri naming.","role":"Regional path topology only; hydrographic figures not digitized.","url":"https://absa.asn.au/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/Cor-Vol-17-Pg135-145_CoralSeaCurrents.pdf"},{"citation":"Oliver and Holbrook (2014), Extending our understanding of South Pacific gyre spin-up: Modeling the East Australian Current in a future climate, doi:10.1002/2013JC009591.","locator":"Section 3: regional SEC bifurcation near 18 S and northward Hiri naming.","role":"Alternative regional origin convention, not a current-core track.","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2013JC009591"},{"citation":"Ganachaud et al. (2014), The Southwest Pacific Ocean circulation and climate experiment (SPICE), doi:10.1002/2013JC009678.","locator":"Section 4.1: NQC, GBRUC and Hiri south of PNG; proposed unified Gulf of Papua Current nomenclature and depth-dependent connections.","role":"Naming-scope caution; does not authorize canonical alias merge.","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2013JC009678"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":1700,"candidate_file":"research/canary-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"b5a8dad9c074d00432e07cb45640469551f1686d3b96e31a4356d0861c7c4309","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","current_id":"canary","figure":"figures/canary-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"canary-reference-path-candidate","name":"Canary Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["CNRY"],"ordering_sensitivity":{"envelope_position_bounds":[14,21],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison.","overlapping_candidate_ids":["north-brazil-reference-path-candidate","labrador-reference-path-candidate","agulhas-reference-path-candidate","somali-winter-reference-path-candidate","alaska-reference-path-candidate","kuroshio-extension-reference-path-candidate","portugal-reference-path-candidate"]},"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_3","remaining_gates":["Review northern feed-region and Cape Blanc naming gates before length admission.","Validate offshore corridor and island clearance using finer coastline, bathymetry and suitable velocity fields.","Resolve source-specific seasonal path and Lanzarote Passage conventions before animated geometry or width extraction.","Canonical admission and publication review; no current footprint or annual extremes inferred."],"route_extent_kind":"Canary offshore return-flow corridor","scenario_count":54,"scenario_range_km":[1500,1800],"scope":"OSW offshore reference corridor from a regional northern source gate near 35 N, past the western Canary archipelago, to a Cape Blanc offshore departure gate near 21 N. Excludes upstream Azores/Portugal routes, the broader Iberian-to-tropical Canary Current System, Lanzarote Passage recirculation, poleward undercurrents and downstream North Equatorial Current. No whole connected-system length.","source_locator":"Section 1 Introduction, first paragraph: distinguishes approximately 35-20 N named-current region from wider Canary Current System; bifurcation away from Africa near Cape Blanc (21 N) toward the North Equatorial Current.","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/971/2018/","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Ibrahim and Sun (2026), A multidecadal sea level rise and its hiatus in the tropical Atlantic margin off northwest Africa, Ocean Science 22, 2059-2081, doi:10.5194/os-22-2059-2026.","locator":"Section 4 opening paragraphs: source-region convergence around 35 N and upper-layer context.","role":"Northern geographic naming-gate context; no model axis digitized.","url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/2059/2026/"},{"citation":"Perez-Hernandez et al. (2023), The Seasonal Cycle of the Eastern Boundary Currents of the North Atlantic Subtropical Gyre, JGR Oceans 128, e2022JC019487.","locator":"Abstract and sections 1-2: regional seasonal migration and distinct Lanzarote Passage flow; Table 1 and prose disagree about fall cruise month.","role":"Seasonal continuity caveat; no 2015 observed axis, section width, transport or annual extrema reconstructed.","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC019487"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":1700,"candidate_file":"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"5ffe93eddca3a110dedfc3a0d2dfb589504d60422e24729e0820629b4a94eafe","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","current_id":"south-indian","figure":"figures/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate","name":"South Indian Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["ISSG","SANT"],"ordering_sensitivity":null,"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_E_5","remaining_gates":["Review the longitude naming transition and exact regional layer against compatible velocity fields.","Resolve the distinction among South Indian Current, South Indian Ocean Current and Agulhas Return under each source convention.","Diagnose meanders and local latitude shifts; the near-40 S editorial connection is not an observed axis.","Resolve the 90 E branching and northeastern continuation independently before any whole-current length.","Recover matching seasonal axes and transverse boundaries before annual length/width ranges."],"route_extent_kind":"eastern regional reach","scenario_count":27,"scenario_range_km":[1600,1800],"scope":"Declared 70 E to 90 E eastern-name-convention regional reach. The west gate follows the later convention reserving South Indian Ocean Current for flow beyond the Agulhas Return Current near 70 E; the east gate is the approximate recirculation/splitting region described in historical hydrography. These are selected regional gates, not whole-current endpoints. Western Agulhas Return, northward recirculation, northeastern Australia continuation and ACC paths are not added. All route latitudes and connecting vertices are editorial.","source_locator":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997), section 3.2 / journal p. 5523 and Figure 7 caption: 90 E recirculation/split and upper-1000 m flow schematic. Later Grand et al. (2015), regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113: SIOC name beyond 70 E. Near-40 S context from Stramma (1992) publisher abstract; drawn latitudes are editorial.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Stramma (1992), The South Indian Ocean Current, JPO 22, 421–430.","locator":"Publisher abstract only: near-40 S STF context and eastern separation beyond 100 E.","supports":"Broad earlier current name and approximate frontal geography; no source centerline digitized.","url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/abstract/journals/phoc/22/4/1520-0485_1992_022_0421_tsioc_2_0_co_2.xml"},{"citation":"Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001), The Agulhas Return Current, Journal of Marine Systems 30, 115–138.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct publisher retrieval returned 403.","supports":"Proposed ARC termination near 66–70 E and SIOC name farther east; source convention, not fixed physical junction.","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924796301000410"},{"citation":"Grand et al. (2015), The impact of circulation and dust deposition in controlling the distributions of dissolved Fe and Al in the south Indian subtropical gyre, Marine Chemistry 176, 110–125.","locator":"Regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113 / PDF page 4.","supports":"SIOC name beyond 70 E; near-90 E recirculation and dispersed eastern flow.","url":"https://science.whoi.edu/users/mcgillic/cruises/TN376/cruiseshare/Morton%20lab/Relevant%20Papers/Grand%20et%20al.%20-%202015%20-%20The%20impact%20of%20circulation%20and%20dust%20deposition%20in%20controlling%20the%20distributions%20of%20dissolved%20Fe%20and%20Al%20in%20the%20south.pdf"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":1700,"candidate_file":"research/tasman-historical-connection-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"f6f60ba8fee67cf1f8163b6f616f664c674e2a7977d36c0d420c0e9c8407a80d","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","current_id":"tasman-front","figure":"figures/tasman-historical-connection-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"tasman-historical-connection-reach-reference-path-candidate","name":"Tasman Front","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["NEWZ","TASM"],"ordering_sensitivity":null,"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_G_5","remaining_gates":["Independently review identity, layer, selected gates and fine coastline/bathymetry before physical admission.","Acquire dated velocity or suitable physical geometry before measuring a current axis or meander length.","Whole-current length, physical width and annual ranges remain unresolved.","No seasonal playback, occupied polygon, physical state containment or NASA current identity inferred."],"route_extent_kind":"historical Tasman reference connection","scenario_count":81,"scenario_range_km":[1600,1800],"scope":"Historical Tasman Front naming convention represented by an OSW offshore 154 E to 172 E near-34 S regional connection. Gates truncate the Australia-northern-New-Zealand geography; neither coastal endpoints nor a continuously identifiable jet is claimed. Excludes coastal EAC, southern extension and East Auckland coastal continuation.","source_locator":"Chapter 8, printed pp127-129 / PDF137-139: Australia-New Zealand connection near 34 S, meanders and statistically defined average position. Version 1.1 March 2005. Cited pages and Figure 8.23 visually inspected.