 or seasonal extrema.","Resolve two-band correspondence within the 115–85 W split region described by Stramma et al. (1995).","Test front-to-flow correspondence against the layered supergyre distinction in Ridgway and Dunn (2007).","Resolve western and eastern continuation independently before a whole-current length or annual width."],"route_extent_kind":"STF-proxy regional reach","scenario_count":27,"scenario_range_km":[1300,1500],"scope":"Declared 103 W to 88 W eastern regional studied reach between two reported Subtropical Front crossings associated with the SPC in the source regional surface circulation. Front locations are proxies, not diagnosed velocity-core endpoints, and were observed in different years. OSW connecting vertices and alternatives are editorial. Branch correspondence is unresolved. Excludes Chatham Rise/western basin, ACC export branch, Peru-Chile coastal flow, northward recirculation and independent split bands. Not a whole-current or simultaneous observed axis.","source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Data [4]–[5], surface circulation [7], STF [14]–[17] and Table 1: P18 at 103 W 33.8 S and P19 at 88 W 34.5 S. Source front/velocity distinction retained; fields and curves not digitized.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2024-12/010047303.pdf","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Stramma, Peterson and Tomczak (1995), The South Pacific Current, JPO 25, 77–91.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct article/PDF access unsuccessful.","supports":"SPC distinction from ACC, broad Chatham Rise context and possible splitting at 115–85 W. Does not assign a branch to this connection.","url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/25/1/1520-0485_1995_025_0077_tspc_2_0_co_2.xml"},{"citation":"Ridgway and Dunn (2007), Observational evidence for a Southern Hemisphere oceanic supergyre, GRL 34, L13612.","locator":"Section 3.4 