ction 4.8, p. 21163: 35 W NEUC centered at 5 N in February 1993 and April 1996; core near sigma-theta 26.75. Sections 4.6 and 6.1 separate source retroflection from the named current; eastern filament context cites earlier work.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt, Claus and Hahn (2020), Fluctuations of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Associated Changes in Oxygen Transports, GRL 47, e2020GL088350, doi:10.1029/2020GL088350.","locator":"Introduction and sections 2–4, pp. 1–4: central 5 N, 23 W observations and 65–270 m definition; data intervals and fixed-box/inferred-transport distinctions.","role":"Central observational context; weak seasonal cycle and episodic intraseasonal events do not establish seasonal geometry.","url":"https://pureadmin.uhi.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/14119479/2020GL088350.pdf"},{"citation":"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt and Duteil (2019), Interannual Variability of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Its Impact on Oxygen, JGR Oceans 124, 2348–2373, doi:10.1029/2018JC014760.","locator":"Introduction, sections 2.1 and 2.3: 23 W ship sections; model half-width and observational integration boundaries.","role":"Distinguishes chosen transport integration widths and model-domain longitude span from diagnosed current dimensions.","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014760"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":1300,"candidate_file":"research/davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"ac2db281859e27e8903fb224f3fdde35b36f010ab111240e2a2c78e3c5a26609","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","current_id":"davidson","figure":"figures/davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a