Islands reference reach","scenario_count":81,"scenario_range_km":[800,1000],"scope":"Editorial eastern Solomon Islands reach between offshore gates near 162.0 E, 9.6 S and 155.8 E, 4.6 S, following island-chain geography toward northeast Bougainville. Excludes the SEC upstream basin, Solomon Strait crossing, New Ireland coastal continuation and EUC. Source descriptions establish regional context; continuity between gates is unresolved. These are OSW truncations, not observed origins or termination.","source_locator":"Melet et al. (2010) coauthor abstract proposes SICU east of Solomon Islands; original model axis not acquired. Ganachaud et al. (2017), Figures 2 and 7 and pages 11-12/17, supply island geography and local observational context, not a continuous SICU axis.","source_url":"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"access":"Original NOAA-hosted PDF acquired and institutional SHA256 matched; CC BY 4.0 printed page 27; selected pages and figures inspected.","label":"Ganachaud et al. (2017), Solomon Sea cruises","locator":"Figures 2 and 7; pages 5-7, 11-12 and 17","url":"https://doi.org/10.1525/elementa.221"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":800,"candidate_file":"research/east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"f4aa14b11d2109ab8df178538e0b954f8431bff833b763fa868f9ba874041455","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","current_id":"east-adriatic","figure":"figures/east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate","name":"East Adriatic Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["MEDI"],"ordering_sensitivity":{"envelope_position_bounds":[25,36],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes o