.","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Urbini et al. (2020), Temporal and Spatial Variability of the CO2 System in a Riverine Influenced Area of the Mediterranean Sea, the Northern Adriatic, doi:10.3389/fmars.2020.00679.","locator":"Study Area, general circulation paragraph: eastern-side northward flow from Otranto toward Istrian Peninsula, citing Poulain (2001).","role":"Regional endpoint convention; not a measured continuous current axis or named termination.","url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2020.00679/full"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":800,"candidate_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"606edd4cfe959e577c65a0a089b607006ed878823af280f113bba682da6af680","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","figure":"figures/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate","name":"East Greenland Coastal Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["SARC"],"ordering_sensitivity":null,"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_B_1","remaining_gates":["Review finer coastline and shelf bathymetry before claiming an inner-shelf current axis.","Resolve northern identification and the 63 N merger before any whole-current extent.","Do not replace the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey description with this shorter editorial reach.","Retain the Cape Farewell 30 km threshold width as a local section; no width buffer or annual footprint inferred."],"route_extent_kind":"66 N–Cape Farewell studied reach","scenario_count":81,"scenario_range_km":[800,900],"scope":"Declared southeast Greenland coastal study-area reach from an OSW offshore gate near 66 N to a Cape Farewell offshore gate near 60 N. Excludes the weak northern 68 N identification, EGC shelfbreak path, Irminger Current, offshore diversions and West Greenland continuation. Not the full EGCC or the source-reported approximately 1000 km surveyed shelf. Near 63 N, the coastal and shelfbreak flows approach or merge; the line does not establish uninterrupted independent coastal flow. The local 30 km Cape Farewell width is not a buffer around this reach.","source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":800,"candidate_file":"research/monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"1074de5de5d68f6ca753a8eafdb2fea5eaecd20204f008c6df156e3c21940f92","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","current_id":"monsoon","figure":"figures/monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate.svg","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","id":"monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate","name":"Monsoon Current","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["MONS"],"ordering_sensitivity":null,"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_E_3","remaining_gates":["Review the regional gate/axis choices against compatible seasonal velocity fields.","Separate surface flow, near-coastal counterflow, equatorial jets and undercurrents.","Resolve upstream and downstream branches before a whole-current estimate.","Recover matching seasonal transverse boundaries and repeat