ected Barents Sea opening northward-departure approach at 73 N, west of Bear Island and Svalbard, to a selected pre-branching gate near 79.6 N. Excludes upstream Norwegian Atlantic routes, eastward Barents inflow, offshore Front Current feeder, westward recirculation, shelf/fjord intrusions and downstream Svalbard/Yermak/Yermak Pass branches. No whole connected Arctic pathway length.","source_locator":"Introduction and Figure 1: Atlantic flow splits between Scandinavia and Svalbard into Barents inflow via Bear Island Trough and northward WSC continuation; shelf/slope components differ.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/2017JC013553","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Menze et al. (2019), Atlantic Water Pathways Along the North-Western Svalbard Shelf Mapped Using Vessel-Mounted Current Profilers, JGR Oceans, doi:10.1029/2018JC014299.","locator":"Abstract; sections 4.3 and 6: northward boundary flow at 79-80 N / 5-10 E, splitting into Svalbard, Yermak and Yermak Pass branches.","role":"Northern branch-region context; summer composite does not establish all branches at every time.","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2018JC014299"},{"citation":"Dundas and Fer (2026), Atlantic Water flow through Fram Strait to the Arctic Ocean measured by repeated glider transects, Ocean Science 22, 1003-1021.","locator":"Introduction; sections 2.1-2.2 and code/data availability: separate slope/front branches, 77.25 N target section and limited season coverage.","role":"Source-specific naming and section/season caveats; transect distances are not current length or width.","url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/1003/2026/"}]},{"approximate_reference_path_km":800,"candidate_file":"research/zeehan-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"454f0a2608695072f6c5ee52452dba34973f0da0b72f646f8d03e6eac1efe2ba","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_referenc