_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"antilles","entity_id":"current:antilles","id":"route-decision:antilles","label":"Antilles Current","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["antilles-northern-bahamas-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"NOAA's six sections near 28°35′N found variable northward and southward bands rather than the broad, persistent northward surface current shown on older charts. This section cannot establish a whole-current path or length and does not resolve flow farther south.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"acquired_profile_context":{"abaco_first_casts":23,"abaco_repeat_casts":27,"depth_samples":22619,"diagnostic_file":"research/antilles-ab0505-400m-section-diagnostic.json","inventory_file":"research/antilles-ab0505-ladcp-profile-inventory.json","inventory_sha256":"491fbe8feb7393600888455c26390d67fe0a734ab2e248d9a0474161a0437227","other_section_casts_excluded":7,"profile_count":57,"provider":"NOAA/AOML/PhOD WBTS","provider_caution_count":17,"provider_usable_count":40,"status":"acquired_profiles_and_derived_one_sided_diagnostic_not_full_width_admission","summary":"At fixed 400 m instrument depth, first May 2005 section is blocked by caution casts. Repeat has about 37 km sampled-peak-to-offshore-half-peak span, not full width. Source quality comments, unremoved tides, error velocities, missing-depth samples and cast times are retained. Whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved."},"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"current_id":"antilles","data_acquisition_review_date":"2026-10-04","date":"2026-10-03","identity_decision":"retain_named_current_with_separate_historical_surface_and_modern_regional_mean_support","length_decision":"whole_current_route_unknown_no_source_defined_endpoints","local_section_support":{"coordinate_role":"nominal_instrument_locations_not_