ate_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"deep-western-boundary","entity_id":"current:deep-western-boundary","id":"route-decision:deep-western-boundary","label":"Deep Western Boundary Current","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"The study identifies southward deep western boundary flow at 47°, 36°, and 24.5°N in decadal inverse solutions. This is a North Atlantic segment only; sections from different cruises do not establish one simultaneous continuous path or a whole-Atlantic current length. The derived floor is unranked.","scope_reviews":[],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk","current_id":"deep-western-boundary","existing_length_evidence_status":"derived_lower_bound","existing_scope":"The study identifies southward deep western boundary flow at 47°, 36°, and 24.5°N in decadal inverse solutions. This is a North Atlantic segment only; sections from different cruises do not establish one simultaneous continuous path or a whole-Atlantic current length. The derived floor is unranked.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"deep western boundary current","name":"Deep Western Boundary Current","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2006GL026965","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","planning_basis":"The study identifies southward deep western boundary flow at 47°, 36°, and 24.5°N in decadal inverse solutions. This is a North Atlantic segment only; sections from different cruises do not establish one simultaneous continuous path or a whole-Atlantic current length. The derived floor is unranked.","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","route_strategy_id":"system_route_graph","route_strategy_label":"Define system and branch graph","strategy_next_action":"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately."},"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2006GL026965","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","strategy_id":"system_route_graph","strategy_label":"Define system and branch graph"},{"candidate_count":1,"construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"east-adriatic","entity_id":"current:east-adriatic","id":"route-decision:east-adriatic","label":"East Adriatic Current","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","candidate_file":"research/east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate.json","current_id":"east-adriatic","exclusions":["Western Adriatic return flow","Northern, central and southern recirculation loops","Individually unverified island-channel branches","Dalmatian-name extent transfer"],"geographic_conventions":[{"access":"publisher_relevant_sections_read","locator":"Section 2.1 and Figure 1","scope":"Northwestward eastern Balkan coast; distinct western return current and recirculation gyres. The stated 800 by 200 km dimensions describe the Adriatic basin, not the EAC length or width.","source_license":"Publisher states Creative Commons Attribution 4.0; no source figure or drifter data copied.","url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/"},{"access":"publisher_relevant_study_area_text_read","locator":"Study area, mean circulation paragraph citing Poulain (2001)","scope":"Background convention extends EAC northward from Otranto toward the Istrian Peninsula. This is regional circulation context, not a diagnosed continuous axis or formal current termination.","source_license":"Not independently reviewed in this audit; attributed textual facts only.","url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2020.00679/full"}],"input_file":"research/east-adriatic-reference-path-input.json","layer":"General surface circulation context in the two accessed papers. Intermediate-water inflow is not assigned the same route or a uniform full-depth layer.","naming_decision":{"assignment":"Editorial alignment of the same eastern-coast northwestward circulation convention; no new canonical alias admitted.","dalmatian_name_synonymy":"unresolved_not_merged","ledger_label":"East Adriatic Current","source_label":"Eastern Adriatic Current"},"observed_period":null,"original_measurement_source":{"access":"Publisher full text inaccessible in this turn; author-hosted search excerpt found but full page access returned HTTP 429. No new values extracted.","citation":"Orlic et al. (2006), Wintertime buoyancy forcing, changing seawater properties, and two different circulation systems produced in the Adriatic.","existing_ledger_scope":"2002-2003 local eastern-coast measurements; no full path length admitted.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2005JC003271"},"proposed_gate_regions":["Eastern Otranto inflow neighborhood","Offshore western/southern Istrian neighborhood"],"remaining_gates":["Choose explicit offshore gate coordinates and alternative coastal paths with the same convention.","Screen all declared paths against the coarse land geometry, then review islands and narrow passages using finer bathymetry.","Retain the regional convention and unresolved Dalmatian naming in every length record; do not borrow 800 km basin length.","Retrieve original measurement and drifter papers before claiming a diagnosed axis, seasonal footprint, or numeric current width."],"route_approximation":{"physical_axis_diagnosed":false,"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":800,"reported_scenario_range_km":[700,800],"scenario_count":81,"source_basin_dimension_not_used":true},"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","source_access":"publisher_full_text_relevant_background_and_figure_caption_read","source_citation":"Sciascia et al. (2018), Linking sardine recruitment in coastal areas to ocean currents using surface drifters and HF radar: a case study in the Gulf of Manfredonia, Adriatic Sea. Ocean Science 14, 1461-1482, doi:10.5194/os-14-1461-2018.","source_locator":"Section 2.1 and Figure 1 caption: northwestward eastern-coast EAC, separate southeastward western-coast WAC, three sub-basin recirculations, wind modulation.","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/east-adriatic-naming-extent-scope-audit.json","current_id":"east-adriatic","label":"East Adriatic naming and extent convention","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Section 2.1 and Figure 1 caption: northwestward eastern-coast EAC, separate southeastward western-coast WAC, three sub-basin recirculations, wind modulation.","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/","summary":"Eastern-coast northwestward circulation convention is distinct from the western return and basin gyres. Otranto-to-Istria context is not a diagnosed whole-current axis; Dalmatian-name overlap remains unresolved, and 800 km basin length is not current length."},"source_sha256":"435ae6d4d1dae6f6a6c4be949d42118efc1158d349584271538ae32ec550c7d1"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate"],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk","current_id":"east-adriatic","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"northwestward coastal boundary current","name":"East Adriatic Current","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2005JC003271","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","planning_basis":"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope",