oastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","input_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-input.json","layer":"Surface-intensified low-salinity inner-shelf jet context from July-August 2004 hydrography and ADCP-referenced geostrophic velocity. No uniform fixed-depth axis diagnosed along this editorial path.","local_width_is_route_buffer":false,"local_width_km":30,"local_width_measurement_id":"east-greenland-coastal-2004-cape-farewell-threshold-section","local_width_velocity_fraction":0.15,"observed_period":null,"remaining_gates":["Review finer coastline and shelf bathymetry before claiming an inner-shelf current axis.","Resolve northern identification and the 63 N merger before any whole-current extent.","Do not replace the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey description with this shorter editorial reach.","Retain the Cape Farewell 30 km threshold width as a local section; no width buffer or annual footprint inferred."],"route_approximation":{"physical_axis_diagnosed":false,"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":800,"reported_scenario_range_km":[800,900],"scenario_count":81},"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Declared southeast Greenland coastal study-area reach from an OSW offshore gate near 66 N to a Cape Farewell offshore gate near 60 N. Excludes the weak northern 68 N identification, EGC shelfbreak path, Irminger Current, offshore diversions and West Greenland continuation. Not the full EGCC or the source-reported approximately 1000 km surveyed shelf. Near 63 N, the coastal and shelfbreak flows approach or merge; the line does not establish uninterrupted independent coastal flow. The local 30 km Cape Farewell width is not a buffer around this reach.","source_access":"Accepted manuscript relevant sections 3, 8 and 9 read; source figure screenshot unavailable; no axis digitized. Width sections 2 and 3.1 inspected in previous extraction.","source_citation":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), The East Greenland Coastal Current: Structure, variability, and forcing, Progress in Oceanography, accepted manuscript.","source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","source_shelf_reach_is_current_axis_length":false,"source_shelf_reach_km":1000,"source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-scope-audit.json","current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","label":"Coastal studied reach, northern uncertainty and local threshold width","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","summary":"The 66 N to Cape Farewell editorial reach is separate from the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey. Weak northern identification and merging near 63 N limit continuity claims. The 30 km Cape Farewell width uses a 15% inner-jet velocity threshold and cannot buffer this whole route or supply annual margins."},"source_sha256":"60349cb57aac6f8602f87b8b88ba3341e39a29cdc603a20aa50d6b9cd92e4ce1"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"component_inv