 No one fixed path or endpoint pair is admitted for a whole-current length.","scope_reviews":[],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["hiri-reference-path-candidate"],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk","current_id":"hiri-current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The literature uses Hiri Current for the northward branch after South Equatorial Current bifurcation off northeast Australia, with variable continuation around the Gulf of Papua. No one fixed path or endpoint pair is admitted for a whole-current length.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"northward western boundary branch and Gulf of Papua circulation","name":"Hiri Current","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2013JC009591","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","planning_basis":"The literature uses Hiri Current for the northward branch after South Equatorial Current bifurcation off northeast Australia, with variable continuation around the Gulf of Papua. No one fixed path or endpoint pair is admitted for a whole-current length.","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents."},"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2013JC009591","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention"},{"candidate_count":1,"construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"indian-equatorial-undercurrent","entity_id":"current:indian-equatorial-undercurrent","id":"route-decision:indian-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"Indian Ocean Equatorial Undercurrent","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"Observed across a 2°S–2°N section at 90°E on 1–3 March 2017; the reported ~13.5 Sv is section transport, not path length. A later review describes the Indian expression as weaker and seasonally varying; one campaign does not establish a permanent path.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","current_id":"indian-equatorial-undercurrent","historical_definition_review":{"august_1994_occurrence_is_universal_season":false,"eastward_subsurface_flow_alone_always_has_undercurrent_structure":false,"local_50_150m_1994_depth_context_applies_to_1963_basin_route":false,"mean_or_instantaneous_definition_requires_review":true,"sampled_longitude_context_east":[53,91],"sampled_period":"March–April 1963, as described from Taft (1967)","sampled_positions_establish_simultaneous_connected_axis":false,"source_locator":"Sections 3.2–3.2.2, printed pp. 28–31; Figure 25 caption p. 30.","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf"},"layer":"2017 reported strong saline eastward band within 80–150 m; not a uniform axis layer or full width at every depth. Historical upper-thermocline definitions can depend on overlying flow.","local_band":{"approximate_meridional_span_km":300,"latitude_limits_are_route_endpoints":false,"measurement_id":"indian-euc-2017-03-described-subsurface-band","source_depth_range_m":[80,150],"source_latitude_limits_degrees":[-1.2,1.5],"span_is_full_width_at_every_depth":false,"survey_latitude_support_degrees":[-2,2],"transport_salinity_domains_are_width_edges":false,"unrounded_meridional_span_km":298.5511199778176,"velocity_threshold_m_s":null},"observed_period":{"end":"2017-03-03","start":"2017-03-01"},"remaining_gates":["Define undercurrent using both subsurface and overlying profiles at each sampled longitude/time.","Recover compatible longitudinal axes before connecting historical positions or measuring whole-current length.","Diagnose transverse velocity edges; reported current/water-mass band limits are a different metric.","Recover repeated compatible dates and sections before seasonal dimensions; one local occurrence cannot define an annual cycle."],"route_construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed_pending_longitudinal_geometry","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Dated local section at 90 E; historical basin observations remain separate from a connected current axis.","source_access":"2019 original six-page PDF text read, including Methods/Results/Conclusions and figure captions; no figure digitized. 2001 original review sections 3.2–3.2.2 and Figure 25 caption read. Original Taft (1967) source not inspected; 2015 Chen et al. full publisher page returned 403 and not used as full-paper evidence.","source_citation":"Siswanto, Kusmanto and McPhaden (2019), Estimated transport of Equatorial Undercurrent observed at 90 E during the Indonesia Prima 2017 campaign, doi:10.1088/1755-1315/303/1/012005.","source_locator":"Data and Methods p. 3; Results p. 4 and Conclusions p. 5. Historical interpretation: Schott/McCreary (2001), sections 3.2–3.2.2, printed pp. 28–31.","source_url":"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/64055/noaa_64055_DS1.pdf","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","time_convention":"Local 1–3 March 2017 section, not recurring seasonal geometry. Historical February–May 1994 and August 1994 occurrences at 80.5 E remain separate evidence.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/indian-euc-dated-band-layer-season-scope-audit.json","current_id":"indian-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"Dated subsurface band and transient undercurrent definition","observed_period":{"end":"2017-03-03","start":"2017-03-01"},"source_locator":"Data and Methods p. 3; Results p. 4 and Conclusions p. 5. Historical interpretation: Schott/McCreary (2001), sections 3.2–3.2.2, printed pp. 28–31.","source_url":"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/64055/noaa_64055_DS1.pdf","summary":"The 1–3 March 2017 section at 90 E describes a roughly 300 km meridional current/salinity band span in the 80–150 m depth range. This is a local descriptive metric, not full width at every depth or along the current. Historical longitudinal samples do not establish one simultaneous axis; overlying flow, transient structure and seasonal exceptions need separate review."},"source_sha256":"c2a0afab6656131ca34d2fee5515258962043c8e7a090d369c24e4cd87ccaf88"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk","current_id":"indian-equatorial-undercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"section_only","existing_scope":"Observed across a 2°S–2°N section at 90°E on 1–3 March 2017; the reported ~13.5 Sv is section transport, not path length. A later review describes the Indian expression as weaker and seasonally varying; one campaign does not establish a permanent path.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"seasonal eastward subsurface jet","name":"Indian Ocean Equatorial Undercurrent","name_source_url":"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/64055","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","planning_basis":"Observed across a 2°S–2°N section at 90°E on 1–3 March 2017; the reported ~13.5 Sv is section transport, not path length. A later review describes the Indian expression as weaker and seasonally varying; one campaign does not establish a permanent path.","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","route_strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","route_strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","strategy_next_action":"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons."},"source_url":"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/64055","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes"},{"candidate_count":1,"construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","entity_id":"current:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","id":"route-decision:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Countercurrent","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"Repeated XBT shipping-line sections identify this flow, including a western line near 55°E with a variable trough around 5–10°S. Section transports and latitude bands are not an along-current length.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","layer":"Surface drifter climatology with GDP drogue support near 15 m and wind-slip-corrected undrogued observations; not a uniform fixed-depth current axis or full vertical extent. OSCAR upper-layer and deeper current diagnostics remain separate.","observed_period":null,"remaining_gates":["Extract the fitted winter velocity field and diagnose current-axis and gate locations.","Resolve source-flow confluence and eastern recirculation/continuation before whole-current length.","Retain drifter sampling bias and uncertainty; drawing offsets do not estimate those errors.","Recover comparable transverse velocity edges and repeat seasonal axes before width or annual extrema."],"route_candidate_file":"research/indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","sampling_context":{"bin_radius_degrees":1,"drogue_support_depth_m":15,"mapped_grid_spacing_degrees":0.25,"months_are_exact_observation_dates":false,"selection_end_month":"2018-10","selection_start_month":"1993-01","simple_bin_average_is_seasonally_unbiased":false,"source_figure_2_sampling_start_discrepancy":"Data selection states 1993 while Figure 2 caption states 1995; retained as unresolved source description."},"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Declared 50-90 E eastward winter surface reach. The 50 E start is an OSW offshore truncation beyond the western confluence, and 90 E follows approximate recirculation context. Neither is a diagnosed whole-current terminus. Excludes Somali/East African source legs, the southern return into SEC, South Java continuation, equatorial Wyrtki jets and subsurface SEUC.","seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"source_access":"Full publisher sections 2 and relevant section 3 seasonal discussion, Figure 5/13 captions and Conclusion inspected. No figure digitized, fitted field acquired or source trajectories traced.","source_citation":"Wu, Du, Qian, Cheng, Wang, Zhang and Peng (2020), Structure and Seasonal Variation of the Indian Ocean Tropical Gyre Based on Surface Drifters, Journal of Geophysical Research: Oceans, doi:10.1029/2019JC015483.","source_locator":"Sections 2.1-2.2: drifter support, 1993-2018 selection, fitted seasonal fields and December-March winter. Section 3 seasonal discussion after Figures 5-6: eastward SECC reaches about 90 E before recirculating into SEC; Figure 13 caption.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2019JC015483","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","time_convention":"Source boreal winter December-March convention; Gauss-Markov seasonal climatology using 1993-2018 drifter context. Not a dated trajectory or complete annual route series.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"width_source_review":{"ORAS5_text_caption_depth_conflict":"Methods says upper 30 m; Figure 2 caption says 0-40 m. No common fixed-depth width assigned.","OSCAR_depth_support_m":[0,30],"access":"Full publisher Introduction, sections 2.1/2.3/2.4/3.1 and Figure 2 caption inspected; no data/contours acquired.","citation":"Huang et al. (2023), Meridional-Width Variability of Near-Equatorial Zonal Currents Along 80.5 E on Seasonal to Interannual Timescales in the Indian Ocean, doi:10.1029/2022JC019147.","frequency_domain_span_is_full_width":false,"late_summer_backflow_implies_same_annual_axis":false,"latitude_limits_degrees":[-6,-2.5],"locator":"Section 3.1 and Figure 2; OSCAR definition in 2.1.","numeric_current_width_km":null,"role":"frequency_amplitude_phase_classification_region_not_paired_velocity_edges","section_longitude_degrees_east":80.5,"source_period_years":[1995,2016],"strongest_eastward_month_context":[3,4],"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC019147","width_edges_diagnosed":false}},"note":{"audit_file":"research/indian-secc-winter-surface-frequency-scope-audit.json","current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Winter surface reach versus spectral section regions","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent"],"source_locator":"Sections 2.1-2.2: drifter support, 1993-2018 selection, fitted seasonal fields and December-March winter. Section 3 seasonal discussion after Figures 5-6: eastward SECC reaches about 90 E before recirculating into SEC; Figure 13 caption.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2019JC015483","summary":"December-March surface drifter context supports the editorial 50-90 E studied reach. A 6-2.5 S frequency/phase classification band at 80.5 E is not paired-edge width. Surface flow stays distinct from the deeper SEUC; whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved.","supporting_sources":[{"access":"Relevant full-text sections inspected; no current edge or width geometry extracted.","label":"Section frequency and phase classification: Huang et al. (2023)","locator":"Sections 2.1 and 3.1, Figure 2 caption","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC019147"}]},"source_sha256":"3f0f00456c54814cfde2c00b97bfa7f34de0c9dace9c293318bfc02327b58606"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk","current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Repeated XBT shipping-line sections identify this flow, including a western line near 55°E with a variable trough around 5–10°S. Section transports and latitude bands are not an along-current length.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"eastward tropical countercurrent","name":"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Countercurrent","name_source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_6/b_fdi_45-46/010007560.pdf","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","planning_basis":"Repeated XBT shipping-line sections identify this flow, including a western line near 55°E with a variable trough around 5–10°S. Section transports and latitude bands are not an along-current length.","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","route_strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","route_strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","strategy_next_action":"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons."},"source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_6/b_fdi_45-46/010007560.pdf","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes"},{"candidate_count":1,"construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","entity_id":"current:indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","id":"route-decision:indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Undercurrent","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"A 10°S, 87°E mooring and reanalysis identify a subsurface eastward jet beneath the westward South Equatorial Current; its deep reach and seasonality differ from the Atlantic flow. No comparable whole-current length is admitted.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","core_width_context":{"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"fixed_depth_width":false,"measurement_id":"indian-seuc-bran-mam-core-spatial-summary","reported_median_km":169,"reported_spatial_range_km":[26,294],"statistic":"median_across_longitudes","strict_threshold_m_s":0.1,"velocity_component":"eastward_zonal_u"},"current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","layer":"BRAN2020 representative isopycnal context 27.9-28.7 sigma0. Source converts this to roughly 300-420 m at the mooring only; not a fixed-depth route throughout the basin.","model_context":{"horizontal_resolution_degrees":0.1,"monthly_climatology_years":[2001,2018],"mooring_depth_conversion_is_uniform_basin_layer":false,"product":"BRAN2020","reference_density_range_sigma0":[27.9,28.7],"season_months":[3,4,5]},"observed_period":null,"remaining_gates":["Extract compatible BRAN density-layer core geometry and review ridge-scale continuity before interpreting the connecting line as an axis.","Resolve source latitude typo (10 N in one paragraph versus 8-10 S elsewhere); southern context is used explicitly.","Review endpoint definitions and extensions before whole-current length.","Recover repeated matched axes and core boundaries before annual length/width extrema or seasonal playback."],"route_candidate_file":"research/indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.","seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"source_access":"Full publisher HTML relevant text and captions inspected; no figure digitized, BRAN field acquired or Supporting Information inspected.","source_citation":"Chen, Han, Zu, Chu and Chen (2022), The Deep-Penetrating South Equatorial Undercurrent in the Tropical South Indian Ocean, Geophysical Research Letters 49, e2022GL098163, doi:10.1029/2022GL098163.","source_consistency_notes":["One Results paragraph prints 10 N; abstract, mooring location and reach discussion give southern latitude. Typo retained as source conflict, not silently corrected.","Methods gives mooring August 2019-May 2020; Figure 1 caption says June 2020. No exact observation endpoint assigned.","Main occurrence January-June and weakening July-August differ from the Discussion January-August wording; this candidate uses March-May only.","Erratum supplies missing Figure 2 units; corrected HTML consulted."],"source_locator":"Sections 2-4, Figures 1-3 captions and Erratum.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","time_convention":"March-May monthly climatological context from 2001-2018 BRAN2020. Not a dated observed axis, annual geometry or a reconstruction of the anomalous 2020 current.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/indian-seuc-mam-layer-core-scope-audit.json","current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"March-May modeled reach and threshold-core spatial width","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Sections 2-4 and Figure 2-3 captions","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163","summary":"March-May BRAN climatology supports a subsurface reach with OSW connecting vertices. Reported threshold-core widths vary across longitudes, not across seasons; density-layer context is separate from the three-dimensional core extent. Whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved. Source latitude and mooring-end-month inconsistencies are retained in the audit."},"source_sha256":"ee9f1525d6a8c0613bcd27f12d70265f0cf953f7f9815c3e625a4cf7b53a7627"}],"source_catalog_file"