esian-throughflow","entity_id":"current:indonesian-throughflow","id":"route-decision:indonesian-throughflow","label":"Indonesian Throughflow","next_action":"Use the source-described network in research/indonesian-throughflow-network-input.json to select individual layer-compatible branches and independently justify gateway/axis conventions. Twelve nodes and fourteen conceptual connections are queryable, with separate exit observations. No sum of branch lengths, scalar whole-system length or physical width follows from connectivity.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":[],"scope":"NASA names the Pacific-to-Indian freshwater passage through narrow gaps of the Maritime Continent but gives no single current centerline or whole-system length. This is a multi-channel flow, so no length enters the ranking.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-04","canonical_taxonomy_admitted":false,"current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","integration_width_caution":"35/35/160 km are transport-integration widths, not current widths. Ombai geographic width is discussed as 37 km in paragraph 8, while transport calculations use 35 km. Neither provides a uniform current footprint.","network_file":"research/indonesian-throughflow-network-input.json","observed_period":{"end_year":2006,"precision":"year","start_year":2004},"rank_eligible":false,"remaining_gates":["Assess full passage/depth coverage and reversals; no complete network asserted.","Recover axes and scientifically justify branch gates before measuring lengths.","Keep upstream and downstream transport budgets separate; no sum over graph edges.","Review original processing and observation gaps before new derived dimensions."],"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","source_access":"Publisher Introduction paragraphs 3–8, Tables 1–2 and section 2.2 read; no figure, field or transport time-series digitized.","source_locator":"Introduction paragraphs 3–4; Tables 1–2; section 2.2.","source_time_caution":"Abstract mentions January 2003; Table 1 explicitly reports 2004–2006 averages. Individual mooring deployment dates differ, including an August 2003 Ombai deployment. Preserve these distinctions.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","status":"source_supported_conceptual_network_not_scientific_taxonomy_admission","summary":"Selected western/eastern inflow and three main exit pathways represented as twelve conceptual nodes and fourteen connections. Three exit transport means retain 2004–2006 support, processing-choice intervals and eight published first-deployment mooring positions. No geographic network edges, full system length, current width, annual extrema or instantaneous one-way-flow claim.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/indonesian-throughflow-network-scope-audit.json","current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","label":"Source-described passage network and exit observations","observed_period":{"end_year":2006,"precision":"year","start_year":2004},"source_locator":"Introduction paragraphs 3–4, Tables 1–2 and section 2.2","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","summary":"Twelve conceptual nodes and fourteen selected passage connections; three 2004–2006 exit transport means and eight published mooring sites. No whole-system length, geographic graph edges or transfer of integration widths to physical current width."},"source_sha256":"a857f6be29353bfb10f79fb91f51466049fc3324cd769d56de44af60e1506a0a"},{"document":{"aliases_resolved":false,"annual_width_range_km":null,"basis_object_sha256":"6f438c549817bd4f0099f727b6244b62fc99ad4a9607e1f3ed1bc89f655e360e","current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","figure":"figures/current-measurement-scopes/indonesian-throughflow.svg","figure_alt":"Measure each passage with explicit depth, period and boundary rules. Channel and transport-integration spans ar