ute-decision:ligurian","label":"Ligurian Current","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"The source describes a Northern Current formed in the Ligurian Sea that flows onward along the Provençal and Balearic slopes; the Ligurian name is treated here as its source-region segment, without assigning the whole system's extent to this record.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"additional_width_evidence_pending_definition_review":{"imperia_coast_distance_limit_range_km":[20,30],"interpretation":"Imperia coast-to-limit range remains unresolved as a width metric. Menton–Nice band is now separately extracted as a local approximately 20 km profile-band span, not paired whole-current width or seasonal margin.","numeric_inventory_admission":false,"source_locator":"Section 4, p. 274 and Discussion p. 276; Fig. 9"},"annual_dimension_ranges":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","current_id":"ligurian","declared_reach_gates":{"downstream":[7.35,43.5],"role":"editorial_neighborhood_truncations_not_formal_named_current_endpoints","upstream":[8.95,44.1]},"excluded_inferences":["No basin-wide recirculation loops added to coastal reach length.","No Corsica feeder path or upstream formation location treated as this gate.","No winter/summer parent widths transferred to local segment.","No broad paper sampling window treated as a continuously observed route."],"layer":"Surface-flow geography in a study combining CODE drifters following the first metre and ARGOSPHERE drifters following the first 10–20 cm with unquantified wind slip. No full-depth or shelf-break axis diagnosed from the editorial route.","naming_reference":{"does_not_establish_osw_segment_convention":true,"endpoint_geometry_present":false,"mrgid":3357,"status":"Proposed standard","url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=3357"},"observed_period":null,"parent_current_id":"northern-mediterranean","parent_scope_note":"The ledger treats Ligurian Current as a Northern Current segment. This studied reach overlaps the broader current geography; do not add its length to the parent or count it as an independent parallel flow.","profile_band_width_extraction":{"approximate_local_span_km":20,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"measurement_id":"ligurian-menton-nice-composite-profile-band","seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"source_current_label":"Northern Current","source_parent_current_id":"northern-mediterranean","source_reported_band_limits_km":[15,35],"span_calculation":"farther_minus_nearer_coast_distance","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical"},"remaining_gates":["Resolve the geographic Ligurian naming convention before whole-segment endpoint admission.","Review source sampling/layer and coastal path with finer bathymetry or compatible current data.","Keep overlapping Northern Current and Ligurian segment lengths separate; do not sum them.","Review local 20 km Menton–Nice profile-band extraction, mixed surface support and remaining Imperia coast-distance limit; no paired whole-current width inferred."],"sampling_context":"Source drifter sampling is intermittent during May–October 2007 and October 2008–January 2009. The selected reach is editorial geographic context, not one float trajectory, simultaneous observation, annual mean or seasonal path.","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","source_access":"primary_pdf_relevant_sections_read","source_citation":"Poulain, Gerin, Rixen, Zanasca, Teixeira, Griffa, Molcard, de Marte and Pinardi (2012), Aspects of the surface circulation in the Liguro-Provencal basin and Gulf of Lion as observed by satellite-tracked drifters (2007–2009), Bollettino di Geofisica Teorica ed Applicata 53(2), 261–279, doi:10.4430/bgta0052.","source_url":"https://mrea.sincem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf","