earch/loop-current-adt-contours-20260925.json","comparison_result":"Highest length-weighted mean speed among 31 eligible gateway-connected ADT contours occurs at 0.62 m ADT. Selected path rounds to 2200 km and is 55.9 km shorter than the NOAA trace before display rounding. This is product/method disagreement, not independent observation, uncertainty or a physical range.","comparison_source_file":"research/gcoos-duacs-loop-20260925.json","current_id":"loop","diagnostic_file":"research/loop-current-dated-streamline-20260925.json","diagnostic_method":"OSW frozen-time velocity integration with strongest northward native-grid seed at an editorial regional gate; distinct from both source contour algorithms","diagnostic_observation_date":"2026-09-25","diagnostic_page":"almanac/loop-current-experiment.html","diagnostic_result":"Nominal gateway-connected path rounds to 2300 km; all four neighboring seed scenarios fail. Integration step changes are small, but no robust range follows from only successful tests.","diagnostic_source_product":"NOAA LSA RADS 4.8.1 Experimental daily absolute surface geostrophic velocities; lacks absolute dynamic topography","method_comparison":{"correlation":0.86,"root_mean_square_difference_km":262},"observed_period":{"end_year":2021,"exact_endpoint_days":null,"start_year":1993},"published_metrics":[{"is_confidence_interval":false,"is_length_of_temporal_mean_path":false,"mean_extension_km":1449,"method":"Demeaned 0.17 m sea-level contour connecting Yucatan Channel and Florida Straits","standard_deviation_km":487},{"is_confidence_interval":false,"is_length_of_temporal_mean_path":false,"mean_extension_km":1495,"method":"Maximum-geostrophic-velocity streamline connecting Yucatan Channel and Florida Straits","standard_deviation_km":466}],"range_interpretation":"Source describes retracted states below 1000 km and extended phases around 1800–2600 km. These are phase descriptions, not an annual extrema range, confidence interval or width.","rank_eligible":false,"recorded_date_comparison_file":"research/loop-current-recorded-date-comparison.json","recorded_date_page":"almanac/loop-current-recorded-dates.html","recorded_date_result":"Predeclared 15 January, April, July and October 2025 snapshots: NOAA connects only on April 15 (1573.2 km), failing at missing velocity on three dates. DUACS selects contours on all four dates (2082.9, 1592.7, 1674.0, 989.4 km); April difference 19.5 km. Four recorded days are not annual extrema, phase labels or a climatology. Preserve product/method failures.","remaining_gates":["Validate gateway placement and section alternatives using geographic and bathymetric evidence","Compatible same-date DUACS ADT acquired through GCOOS; recover original supplemental maximum-velocity algorithm and compare its gateway/method choices","Preserve failed seed outcomes and assess effective resolution and grid masks","Four predeclared dates tested; assess original method/gateway choices and broader repeated-date coverage before describing physical variability or seasonal ranges","Complete scientific and regional raw-subset source-use review before admission/publication"],"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","source_access":"Full publisher HTML methods and results read. Figures were not digitized. Supplemental numerical Loop Current paths were not acquired.","source_citation":"Manta et al. (2023), Predicting the Loop Current dynamics combining altimetry and deep flow measurements through the Yucatan Channel, Frontiers in Marine Science 10:1156159, doi:10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159.","source_locators":["Sections 2.2, 3.1, 4.1; Figures 1C and 2A captions"],"source_product":"Copernicus DUACS DT-2018 daily 0.25-degree absolute dynamic topography and surface geostrophic velocity","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159/full","status":"editorial_source_and_diagnostic_summary_not_canonical","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/loop-current-altimetry-method-scope-audit.json","current_id":"loop","label":"Dated open-path methods and ADT comparison","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Sections 2.2, 3.1 and 4.1; local pinned 25 September 2026 experiments","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159/full","summary":"Five dated NOAA/DUACS comparisons are retained. For four predeclared 2025 dates, NOAA connects only in April; its other nominal traces stop at missing velocities. DUACS supplies four contours; April method difference is 19.5 km. The September 2026 comparison and failed neighbors remain available. Shared inputs, gates and sparse date coverage prevent treating these as independent confirmation, annual extrema, widths or ranked whole-current lengths."},"source_sha256":"807d7901af9483625b6d3074d7edefcf46b410284217c5a1f7a99f60c4a36d7f"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk","current_id":"loop","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The loop expands and retracts; its path length changes.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"western boundary current segment","name":"Loop Current","name_source_url":"https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/loopcurrent.html","next_action":"Review regional gateway placement, effective resolution and original maximum-velocity contour details against five dated NOAA/DUACS comparisons. Four predeclared 2025 dates retain three failed nominal NOAA traces, while DUACS remains connected. Assess broader observed regimes; failed methods and sparse snapshots do not establish annual ranges. See research/loop-current-recorded-date-comparison.json; no ranked length or width admitted.","planning_basis":"The loop expands and retracts; its path length changes.","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"reference_path_decision":"reference_path_not_constructed","route_strategy_id":"dated_geometry","route_strategy_label":"Construct dated or regime-specific geometry","strategy_next_action":"Use dated or explicitly averaged geometry, distinguish an open loop from a closed circuit, and compare repeated regimes before summarizing."},"source_url":"https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/loopcurrent.html","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","strategy_id":"dated_geometry","strategy_label":"Construct dated or regime-specific geometry"},{"candidate_count":1,"construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"mauritanian","entity_id":"current:mauritanian","id":"route-decision:mauritanian","label":"Mauritanian Current","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["mauritanian-summer-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"The source reports poleward surface flow during the May–July relaxation season in the Mauritanian upwelling region; winter upwelling-season coastal flow is equatorward. A single year-round direction or whole-current length would misrepresent this seasonal regime.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"current_id":"mauritanian","excluded_cruise":"M129 August 2016 excluded from both means","fixed_depth_width":false,"observed_period":null,"relaxation_season_months":[5,6,7],"remaining_gates":["Recover layer-compatible paired edges and field axes with sampling support.","Resolve along-coast and relaxation-season dimensions; preserve annual gaps.","Independent scientific identity/measurement admission."],"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Reference 18 N seasonal mean section; local measurements pooled from 17–19 N via reference topography.","seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"source_access":"Publisher Introduction, section 2.1/Table 2, section 3.1/Figures 4–5 captions, Discussion and Conclusion read. No figure digitization, raw fields or underlying cruise reports acquired.","source_conflict":"Introduction cites Kounta coastal-wave passage to 20 S despite northward context; not interpreted as a geographic current endpoint.","source_naming_rule":"Authors propose Mauritania Current for both poleward surface and undercurrent manifestations. Equatorward shelf surface flow is a separate opposing feature, not a reversal of the entire named poleward flow.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-03","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014264","source_width_range_km":[30,40],"status":"editorial_source_scope_not_scientific_approval","surface_200_km_context_is_width":false,"transport_window_is_width":false,"upwelling_season_months":[12,1,2,3,4],"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"width_edges_extracted":false,"width_record_id":"mauritanian-upwelling-seasonal-mean-width-range","width_role":"author_reported_span_of_upwelling_season_mean_undercurrent"},"note":{"audit_file":"research/mauritanian-seasonal-mean-scope-audit.json","current_id":"mauritanian","label":"Poleward surface/undercurrent manifestations and seasonal mean width","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Sections 2.1, 3.1, 4 and 5; Table 2 and Figure 5 caption.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014264","summary":"At reference 18 N, the study names poleward surface and subsurface manifestations Mauritania Current. Its 30–40 km upwelling-season mean undercurrent width is local; the equatorward shelf jet, transport window and broader surface corridor are separate. No whole-current route or annual wi