_name_not_new_canonical_current"},{"calendar_months":[11,12,1,2],"flow_direction":"westward","label":"Northeast Monsoon Current","source_label_role":"seasonal_phase_under_existing_name_not_new_canonical_current"}],"source_access":"Original review PDF section 5.1.5 and Figure 48 caption read. Schott et al. (1994) publisher-indexed abstract read; direct full article retrieval failed. No figure, model curve or velocity field digitized.","source_citation":"Schott and McCreary (2001), The monsoon circulation of the Indian Ocean, Progress in Oceanography 51, 1–123, doi:10.1016/S0079-6611(01)00083-0.","source_locator":"Section 5.1.5, printed pp. 63–65 / PDF indices 62–64; Figure 48 caption distinguishes August 1993 and January 1991 sections.","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Schott, Reppin, Fischer and Quadfasel (1994), Currents and transports of the Monsoon Current south of Sri Lanka.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct full article unavailable.","supports":"Local mooring/ship observations distinguish shallow surface flow, seasonal reversal and nearby opposite flow. Transport integration support is not a longitudinal route or complete transverse width.","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1029/94JC02216"}],"time_convention":"Boreal source labels, June–September SMC and November–February NMC. Transition geometry is missing; reported persistence beyond February is not forced into the nominal winter calendar.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/monsoon-sri-lanka-seasonal-layer-scope-audit.json","current_id":"monsoon","label":"Seasonal reversal, shallow layers and counterflows","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Section 5.1.5, printed pp. 63–65 / PDF indices 62–64; Figure 48 caption distinguishes August 1993 and January 1991 sections.","source_url":"https