moved; upper-400 m instrument outage July 2016–March 2017. Monthly averages; three cycles provide limited independence.","schema":"osw.current-seasonal-direction-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Local alongshore direction at the 141.4 E, 1.7 S mooring; monthly composite of three cycles, with interannual contamination and instrument gaps. Not a whole-current monthly path.","source_access":"Publisher abstract, Introduction, Data and Method, sections 3.1–3.3 and figure captions read. No figure, velocity field or axis digitized.","source_citation":"Zhang et al. (2020), Seasonal and Interannual Variability of the Currents off the New Guinea Coast From Mooring Measurements, doi:10.1029/2020JC016242.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242","status":"editorial_source_summary_not_canonical","time_precision":"month","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-current-seasonal-direction-scope-audit.json","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","label":"Local seasonal direction and El Niño exception","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent"],"source_locator":"Data and Method, sections 3.2–3.3 / Figures 4 and 9 captions","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242","summary":"Local upper-ocean direction composite reverses southeastward November–April to northwestward May–October. Three-cycle sampling, gaps and El Niño exceptions limit annual interpretation. Direction symbols are not current axes or measured seasonal lengths/widths."},"source_sha256":"8b5fc2d62a5a7c777b69106aa7875260d52bbdff9a2059fbe06d6a1d364652fc"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-surface-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"component_invent