Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"The source describes northwestward flow along Papua New Guinea and through Vitiaz Strait into the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent source region. It gives no comparable whole-current centerline length.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","candidate_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.json","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","input_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-input.json","layer":"Subsurface thermocline flow. Ueki et al. report a local northwestward core generally at 150â€“250 m near the moorings; the core shoals during El Nino. This local depth support is not a fixed-depth axis assigned along the entire editorial reach. Surface New Guinea Coastal Current remains a separate identity.","observed_period":null,"remaining_gates":["Review finer coastline and bathymetry before claiming a subsurface coastal axis.","Resolve upstream branch convention, gateway passages and downstream equatorial connection separately.","Local 150â€“250 m core cannot establish a uniform fixed-depth path, and surface monsoon reversal cannot be transferred to the undercurrent.","Obtain comparable dated geometry or cross-flow sections before annual length/width margins."],"route_approximation":{"physical_axis_diagnosed":false,"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":600,"reported_scenario_range_km":[500,700],"scenario_count":81},"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Declared north-Papua New Guinea regional reach from an OSW offshore Vitiaz-downstream approach gate near 147 E, 4.5 S to the 142 E, 2.5 S mooring neighborhood. Excludes passage through Vitiaz Strait itself, upstream Solomon Sea coastal branches, New Britain and St Georges branches, and the cross-equatorial EUC connection. Gates do not establish whole-current origin or termination.","source_access":"Relevant publisher introduction, Data [8]–[10], Table 1 and Results [17]–[18] read; figures and ADCP fields not digitized.","source_citation":"Ueki, Kashino and Kuroda (2003), Observation of current variations off the New Guinea coast including the 1997â€“1998 El Nino period and their relationship with Sverdrup transport, Journal of Geophysical Research: Oceans, doi:10.1029/2002JC001611.","source_local_core_depth_context_m":[150,250],"source_local_core_is_uniform_route_layer":false,"source_locator":"Ueki et al. (2003), Introduction [2]â€“[7]: separate surface and thermocline flows, northern PNG coast and gateway relations; Data [8]: 142 E moorings; Results 3.1 [17]â€“[18]: local 150â€“250 m core and El Nino shoaling. Relevant text inspected; no current axis digitized.","source_mooring_locations_are_route_endpoints":false,"source_mooring_locations_lon_lat":[[142,-2],[142,-2.5]],"source_sampling_context":"Two upward-looking 150-kHz ADCP moorings; changing sampled depth bounds approximately 30–50 to 200–330 m, subsampled at 10 m intervals. Not uniform vertical support along route.","source_season_convention":{"label_basis":"boreal","months_by_label":{"fall":[10,11,12],"summer":[7,8,9],"winter":[1,2,3]},"role":"source_observation_labels_only","source_locator":"Ueki et al. (2003), Data [10], Table 1 footnote: source defines Northern Hemisphere season labels and month windows.","supports_annual_route_geometry":false},"source_seasonality_scope":"Local undercurrent remains northwestward with boreal summer intensification in the record, with ENSO-related shoaling. Surface current reversal is a separate current. No annual geometry series extracted.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2002JC001611","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-layer-season-scope-audit.json","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","label":"Subsurface PNG reach, mooring support and boreal source seasons","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Ueki et al. (2003), Introduction [2]â€“[7]: separate surface and thermocline flows, northern PNG coast and gateway relations; Data [8]: 142 E moorings; Results 3.1 [17]â€“[18]: local 150â€“250 m core and El Nino shoaling. Relevant text inspected; no current axis digitized.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2002JC001611","summary":"Northern PNG editorial reach is separate from the seasonally reversing surface New Guinea Coastal Current. The source uses boreal labels south of the equator; its local 150–250 m undercurrent core and ENSO shoaling do not provide annual path or width geometry. Vitiaz passage, other branches and downstream EUC lengths are excluded."},"source_sha256":"44153b6d41d13880780d4583255e276a9f69278db88ff2204caead1cb5abf22e"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate"],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk","current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The source describes northwestward flow along Papua New Guinea and through Vitiaz Strait into the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent source region. It gives no comparable whole-current centerline length.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"northwestward subsurface western boundary current","name":"New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2