-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.json","current_id":"new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent","input_file":"research/new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-input.json","layer":"Subsurface thermocline boundary-current geography. Grenier et al. discuss density-dependent modeled pathways; no single fixed-depth axis or whole-depth current footprint extracted for this coastal reach.","observed_period":null,"other_source_access":[{"access":"Publisher page returned internal retrieval error; no additional numeric extraction.","role":"Future observed-pathway corroboration","url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/46/10/jpo-d-16-0107.1.xml"}],"remaining_gates":["Review finer island coastline and bathymetry before claiming a subsurface coastal axis.","Resolve northern branching and southern entrance convention before whole-current extent.","Source model closes St Georges Channel at this resolution; do not infer that channel is physically absent.","Do not transfer source EUC dimensions or gateway section dimensions to the NICU."],"route_approximation":{"physical_axis_diagnosed":false,"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":400,"reported_scenario_range_km":[300,500],"scenario_count":81,"source_particle_paths_digitized":false},"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Declared regional east-coast New Ireland reach from an OSW southeastern offshore gate near 153.6 E, 4.5 S to an OSW northern offshore gate near 150.9 E, 2.2 S. Excludes Solomon Strait inflow across the basin, New Britain and St Georges branches, Bismarck Sea westward continuation, retroflection and downstream EUC route. Gates are editorial truncations, not whole-current origin or termination.","source_access":"Publisher relevant introduction, model description/validation and pathway discussion read; no full-article read or source geometry digitization claimed.","source_citation":"Grenier et al. (2011), From