oast and represents it with stations 1 and 5 nautical miles off Torungen; this is a section location, not a whole-current length. Its relation to the name Norwegian Current is convention-dependent.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"low-salinity coastal current","name":"Norwegian Coastal Current","name_source_url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=2364","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","planning_basis":"A source identifies the current along the Norwegian coast and represents it with stations 1 and 5 nautical miles off Torungen; this is a section location, not a whole-current length. Its relation to the name Norwegian Current is convention-dependent.","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents."},"source_url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=2364","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention"},{"candidate_count":0,"construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","current_id":"norwegian","entity_id":"current:norwegian","id":"route-decision:norwegian","label":"Norwegian Current","next_action":"Resolve source naming and branch extent before route construction; no transfer of neighboring current dimensions. See research/norwegian-naming-branch-scope-audit.json.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":[],"scope":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet. Published usage of this name overlaps with, or distinguishes it from, the Norwegian Coastal Current; identity remains unresolved here.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","current_id":"norwegian","name_equivalence_admitted":false,"observed_period":null,"proposed_identity_ids":["norwegian-atlantic","norwegian-atlantic-slope","norwegian-atlantic-front"],"related_current_ids":["norwegian-coastal"],"remaining_gates":["Resolve naming convention using direct source definitions before transferring route geometry.","Retain distinct salinity, layer, branch and temporal scope.","No numeric dimensions, footprint or seasonal cycle inferred from nearby currents."],"route_construction_status":"identity_scope_unresolved","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","source_access":"Relevant current glossary entries read; not full glossary read.","source_locator":"Norwegian Current, North Atlantic Current and Spitsbergen Atlantic Current entries.","source_metric_caveats":"Source 50 km heat-budget box width is a modeling choice; 750 km Gimsøy–Bjørnøya path is a segment convention. Neither transferred to the Norwegian Current. Static 50%-mean-transport core differs from a dated full-current width.","source_sampling_context":"1993–2022 repeated CTD sections plus satellite surface geostrophic reference; not an observation date for the ambiguous Norwegian Current.","source_url":"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","summary":"NOAA Norwegian Current is a broad northeastward off-Norway naming convention. The modern Norwegian Atlantic Current, with separate slope and front branches, is not automatically this ledger identity or the Norwegian Coastal Current. Name equivalence remains unresolved; whole-current dimensions remain unknown.","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Baumann, Skagseth, Ingvaldsen and Mork (2026), Reduced cooling in the Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current: investigating mechanisms of change from 30 years of observations, Ocean Science 22, 17–29, doi:10.5194/os-22-17-2026.","locator":"Introduction: two Atlantic branches and northern bifurcation; sections 2.1–2.1.2: sampling/core criteria.","source_access":"Relevant introduction and methods read.","source_license":"CC BY 4.0","url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/17/2026/"}],"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/norwegian-naming-branch-scope-audit.json","current_id":"norwegian","label":"Naming convention and Atlantic branch scope","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["norwegian-coastal"],"source_locator":"Norwegian Current, North Atlantic Current and Spitsbergen Atlantic Current entries.","source_url":"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary","summary":"NOAA Norwegian Current is a broad northeastward off-Norway naming convention. The modern Norwegian Atlantic Current, with separate slope and front branches, is not automatically this ledger identity or the Norwegian Coastal Current. Name equivalence remains unresolved; whole-current dimensions remain unknown."},"source_sha256":"b191cb19d5fe5d82b786fb8bdcd3f4b1ffd7c251add3430c10b6e09d4acf2d9f"},{"document":{"aliases_resolved":false,"annual_width_range_km":null,"basis_object_sha256":"854038e0d691b2719599b8a63bee7b1251f7bc7be29d4d6a37d943d9255877b5","current_id":"norwegian","figure":"figures/current-measurement-scopes/norwegian.svg","figure_alt":"Resolve the source-specific name and branch convention before attaching a width. Related records are not confirmed aliases or members. Relationships only; member measurements are not inherited.","generator_file":"analysis/build_current_measurement_scopes.py","generator_sha256":"1357a690e4780eff266db7e95c1998498df88f1e76fdff570b2676d78528534f","member_measurements_inherited":false,"members":[{"id":"norwegian-coastal","label":"Norwegian Coastal Current","record_status":"released","relations