North Equatorial Countercurrent","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"Repeated Pacific velocity sections identify a near-surface eastward core around 7°N at 140°W. The section locates the current but gives no comparable along-current length.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-04","candidate_file":"research/pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","current_id":"pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent","editorial_latitude_choices":{"110W":6,"95W":7},"layer":"Near-surface and upper-ocean eastward countercurrent; maxima can be slightly subsurface. Separate from equatorial EUC and deeper NSCC/Tsuchiya Jet; no uniform depth imposed.","local_section_diagnostic":{"file":"research/pacific-necc-oscar-2013-section-diagnostic.json","scope":"140 W archived OSCAR monthly means in 2013; not a whole-current width or reproduction of the source climatology.","status":"derived_width_candidate_requires_scientific_review","visual_url":"almanac/necc-section.html"},"observed_period":null,"remaining_gates":["Review editor-selected 110 W/95 W latitudes and interpolating continuity against compatible velocity fields.","Extract depth and month-specific axes before length or width seasonal ranges.","Keep weak or absent surface flow near 110 W separate from subsurface eastward flow; no annual continuous path inferred.","Resolve western inflow and coastal redistribution separately from this truncated studied reach."],"route_construction_status":"editorial_studied_reach_constructed","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Declared east-central Pacific study reach from 140 W to 95 W. Gates truncate a larger current; western Pacific inflow and coastal redistribution east of 95 W are excluded. Intermediate bends are editorial connections among section descriptions, not a reconstructed continuous axis or parcel trajectory.","section_longitudes_degrees_east":[-140,-125,-110,-95],"section_mapping_caution":"ADCP generally begins about 20 m; mapped shear is extrapolated to surface. The source uses annual harmonics/SOI with uneven sampling, not monthly routes extracted here.","source_access":"NOAA-hosted introduction, section 2 and section 3 text read; figures and CTD/ADCP fields not digitized or repackaged. Bibliographic page range 31-61 checked against PMEL publication record; HTML header 31-36 is not adopted.","source_citation":"Johnson, Sloyan, Kessler and McTaggart (2002), Direct measurements of upper ocean currents and water properties across the tropical Pacific during the 1990s, Progress in Oceanography 52, 31-61, doi:10.1016/S0079-6611(02)00021-6.","source_declared_correlation_scales_are_width":false,"source_ensemble_period_is_route_date":false,"source_ensemble_period_months":{"end":"2000-12","start":"1985-06"},"source_locator":"Section 3.1: 140 W near-surface core around 7 N, 125 W around 8 N, southward shift at 110 W and northward rebuilding at 95 W; section 3.2.3 separates seasonal surface expression near 110 W.","source_url":"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","surface_expression_caution":"Near 110 W the fitted source surface expression is absent in December-February and peaks in August; slightly subsurface maxima and NSCC are distinct. No general absence of all eastward upper-ocean flow is claimed.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/pacific-necc-reach-seasonal-section-scope-audit.json","current_id":"pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Mean section connection versus seasonal surface expression","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Section 3.1: 140 W near-surface core around 7 N, 125 W around 8 N, 