ing-array support and branch intermittency; do not transfer northern Tsuchiya Jet length or local depths.","Resolve branch-specific intermediate geometry before a route length.","Do not treat 8.5-17.5 N integration span as width or 900 m integration endpoint as core depth."],"route_construction_status":"intermediate_branch_geometry_required","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","source_access":"Abstract and relevant mean-structure and limitations paragraphs read. Mooring figures and fields not digitized.","source_locator":"Mean structure Results: 130 E multiple eastward jets at 8.5 N/12.5 N/17.5 N; positive velocities integrated from 26.8 sigma-theta to 900 m across 8.5-17.5 N.","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.979442/full","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","transport_integration_bounds_are_current_width":false,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/pacific-neuc-nscc-distinction-scope-audit.json","current_id":"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"NEUC mooring jets versus northern Tsuchiya support","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Mean structure Results: 130 E multiple eastward jets at 8.5 N/12.5 N/17.5 N; positive velocities integrated from 26.8 sigma-theta to 900 m across 8.5-17.5 N.","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.979442/full","summary":"The 130 E NEUC mooring study concerns multiple subsurface jets farther north than the equatorial northern Tsuchiya cores. No alias equivalence or connecting trajectory is established; the Tsuchiya route length is not transferred. Transport integration bounds do not establish width."},"source_sha256":"d41b02c0c981c39afacbecb50b67ee4b9613d691a226c0f980063a830682b564"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599