 identities before route construction."},"source_url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=5391","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","strategy_id":"split_basin_family","strategy_label":"Split basin families"},{"candidate_count":1,"construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"south-indian","entity_id":"current:south-indian","id":"route-decision:south-indian","label":"South Indian Current","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"Eastward subtropical-gyre flow near 40 degrees S in the cited study; no source-defined whole-current path length admitted. Do not conflate with the Agulhas Return Current or offshore West Australian Current. Cartographic crossings remain separately pending review.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","candidate_file":"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","current_id":"south-indian","input_file":"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-input.json","latitudes_are_editorial":true,"layer":"Historical upper-1000 m geostrophic transport context, not a uniform-depth velocity axis or surface trajectory. Variable deep reference surfaces affect diagnosed transport; no layer-specific centerline reconstructed.","longitude_gates_are_exact_physical_junctions":false,"name_equivalence_status":"Source-convention interpretation under existing South Indian ledger record; no universal alias equivalence established.","naming_conventions":[{"extent_convention":"Broad eastward southern-gyre flow, including western transport context.","physical_endpoints_established":false,"source":"Stramma (1992); Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997)"},{"extent_convention":"Retain SIOC name beyond ARC termination near 66–70 E; eastern regional flow weak/dispersed.","physical_endpoints_established":false,"source":"Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001); Grand et al. (2015)"}],"observed_period":null,"remaining_gates":["Review the longitude naming transition and exact regional layer against compatible velocity fields.","Resolve the distinction among South Indian Current, South Indian Ocean Current and Agulhas Return under each source convention.","Diagnose meanders and local latitude shifts; the near-40 S editorial connection is not an observed axis.","Resolve the 90 E branching and northeastern continuation independently before any whole-current length.","Recover matching seasonal axes and transverse boundaries before annual length/width ranges."],"route_approximation":{"physical_axis_diagnosed":false,"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":1700,"reported_scenario_range_km":[1600,1800],"scenario_count":27},"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Declared 70 E to 90 E eastern-name-convention regional reach. The west gate follows the later convention reserving South Indian Ocean Current for flow beyond the Agulhas Return Current near 70 E; the east gate is the approximate recirculation/splitting region described in historical hydrography. These are selected regional gates, not whole-current endpoints. Western Agulhas Return, northward recirculation, northeastern Australia continuation and ACC paths are not added. All route latitudes and connecting vertices are editorial.","source_access":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997) PDF Introduction, Methods and section 3.2 / Figure 7 caption read; Grand et al. (2015) PDF section 3.1.1 read. Stramma (1992) publisher abstract read. Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001) publisher-indexed abstract available; direct publisher page returned 403. No source figure or field digitized.","source_citation":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997), The flow field of the subtropical gyre of the South Indian Ocean, JGR 102, 5513–5530, doi:10.1029/96JC03455.","source_locator":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997), section 3.2 / journal p. 5523 and Figure 7 caption: 90 E recirculation/split and upper-1000 m flow schematic. Later Grand et al. (2015), regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113: SIOC name beyond 70 E. Near-40 S context from Stramma (1992) publisher abstract; drawn latitudes are editorial.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Stramma (1992), The South Indian Ocean Current, JPO 22, 421–430.","locator":"Publisher abstract only: near-40 S STF context and eastern separation beyond 100 E.","supports":"Broad earlier current name and approximate frontal geography; no source centerline digitized.","url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/abstract/journals/phoc/22/4/1520-0485_1992_022_0421_tsioc_2_0_co_2.xml"},{"citation":"Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001), The Agulhas Return Current, Journal of Marine Systems 30, 115–138.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct publisher retrieval returned 403.","supports":"Proposed ARC termination near 66–70 E and SIOC name farther east; source convention, not fixed physical junction.","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924796301000410"},{"citation":"Grand et al. (2015), The impact of circulation and dust deposition in controlling the distributions of dissolved Fe and Al in the south Indian subtropical gyre, Marine Chemistry 176, 110–125.","locator":"Regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113 / PDF page 4.","supports":"SIOC name beyond 70 E; near-90 E recirculation and dispersed eastern flow.","url":"https://science.whoi.edu/users/mcgillic/cruises/TN376/cruiseshare/Morton%20lab/Relevant%20Papers/Grand%20et%20al.%20-%202015%20-%20The%20impact%20of%20circulation%20and%20dust%20deposition%20in%20controlling%20the%20distributions%20of%20dissolved%20Fe%20and%20Al%20in%20the%20south.pdf"}],"time_convention":"Editorial regional connection informed by historical hydrographic mean-flow context and source naming conventions. Not a simultaneous observation, monthly climatological axis or annual geometry.","upper_1000m_transport_is_uniform_axis_layer":false,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-naming-layer-scope-audit.json","current_id":"south-indian","label":"Eastern naming convention and idealized transport reach","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["agulhas-return"],"source_locator":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997) section 3.2; Grand et al. (2015) section 3.1.1; earlier/later naming conventions retained.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455","summary":"70–90 E is a declared regional reach under the eastern SIOC naming convention. Longitude gates are approximate context, and every latitude/connecting bend is editorial. Historical upper-1000 m transport is not a fixed-depth axis; western ARC, recirculation and northeastern continuation are not summed. Whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved."},"source_sha256":"0321bf4f204390217073f2e6d319e37e04e4f9dbd3a23e555a76a17a80c0919e"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk","current_id":"south-indian","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Eastward subtropical-gyre flow near 40 degrees S in the cited study; no source-defined whole-current path length admitted. Do not conflate with the Agulhas Return Current or offshore West Australian Current. Cartographic crossings remain separately pending review.","known_component_currents":[],"ledger_kind":"basin-spanning current","name":"South Indian Current","name_source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2014gb004898","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","planning_basis":"Eastward subtropical-gyre flow near 40 degrees S in the cited study; no source-defined whole-current path length admitted. Do not conflate with the Agulhas Return Current or offshore West Australian Current. Cartographic crossings remain separately pending review.","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents."},"source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2014gb004898","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention"},{"candidate_count":1,"construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","current_id":"south-pacific","entity_id":"current:south-pacific","id":"route-decision:south-pacific","label":"South Pacific Current","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","rank_eligible":false,"route_ids":["south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"scope":"Named eastward current associated with the South Pacific subtropical front; map arrows do not measure its full length.","scope_reviews":[{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"as_of":"2026-10-03","branch_correspondence":"unresolved in the source 115–85 W splitting region","candidate_file":"research/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","crossings_form_simultaneous_geometry":false,"current_id":"south-pacific","frontal_crossings_are_velocity_core_locations":false,"input_file":"research/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-input.json","layer":"Surface drifter circulation context combined with separate hydrographic STF crossing locations. The 14 C at 150 m frontal criterion does not define a 150 m current axis; drifter velocities include ageostrophic flow. No fixed-depth velocity centerline reconstructed.","observed_period":null,"remaining_gates":["Diagnose a same-layer velocity axis; frontal proxy locations are not current-core locations.","Recover compatible simultaneous observations before a dated route or seasonal extrema.","Resolve two-band correspondence within the 115–85 W split region described by Stramma et al. (1995).","Test front-to-flow correspondence against the layered supergyre distinction in Ridgway and Dunn (2007).","Resolve western and eastern continuation independently before a whole-current length or annual width."],"route_approximation":{"physical_axis_diagnosed":false,"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":1400,"reported_scenario_range_km":[1300,1500],"scenario_count":27},"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Declared 103 W to 88 W eastern regional studied reach between two reported Subtropical Front crossings associated with the SPC in the source regional surface circulation. Front locations are proxies, not diagnosed velocity-core endpoints, and were observed in different years. OSW connecting vertices and alternatives are editorial. Branch correspondence is unresolved. Excludes Chatham Rise/western basin, ACC export branch, Peru-Chile coastal flow, northward recirculation and independent split bands. Not a whole-current or simultaneous observed axis.","source_150m_temperature_criterion_is_axis_layer":false,"source_access":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005) repository PDF Data, sections 3.1–3.3, Table 1 text and summary read. Stramma et al. (1995) publisher-indexed abstract read; direct article/PDF access unsuccessful. Ridgway and Dunn (2007) publisher section 3.4 [15] read. No figure/velocity curve digitized.","source_anchor_observations":[{"geometry_role":"observed_front_crossing_not_current_axis","id":"p18-1994-stf-crossing","longitude_latitude":[-103,-33.8],"observed_period":{"end":"1994-04","start":"1994-02"},"source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Table 1 / Data [5]: P18 103 W 33.8 S.","time_precision":"month"},{"geometry_role":"observed_front_crossing_not_current_axis","id":"p19-1993-stf-crossing","longitude_latitude":[-88,-34.5],"observed_period":{"end":"1993-04","start":"1993-02"},"source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Table 1 / Data [5]: P19 88 W 34.5 S.","time_precision":"month"}],"source_citation":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Surface circulation and fronts of the South Pacific Ocean, east of 120 W, Geophysical Research Letters 32, L08605, doi:10.1029/2004GL022070.","source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Data [4]–[5], surface circulation [7], STF [14]–[17] and Table 1: P18 at 103 W 33.8 S and P19 at 88 W 34.5 S. Source front/velocity distinction retained; fields and curves not digitized.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2024-12/010047303.pdf","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","supporting_sources":[{"citation":"Stramma, Peterson and Tomczak (1995), The South Pacific Current, JPO 25, 77–91.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct article/PDF access unsuccessful.","supports":"SPC distinction from ACC, broad Chatham Rise context and possible splitting at 115–85 W. Does not assign a branch to this connection.","url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/25/1/1520-0485_1995_025_0077_tspc_2_0_co_2.xml"},{"citation":"Ridgway and Dunn (2007), Observational evidence for a Southern Hemisphere oceanic supergyre, GRL 34, L13612.","locator":"Section 3.4 [15]: gyre return flow and STF relation.","supports":"Layered gyre return flow is not universally identified by the STF; no whole-current or intermediate-layer axis copied from surface/frontal proxies.","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2007GL030392"}],"time_convention":"1979–2004 regional drifter mean is context; P18 frontal crossing was sampled February–April 1994 and P19 February–April 1993. This editorial connection does not combine them into one dated trajectory or infer seasonal geometry.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-layer-time-scope-audit.json","current_id":"south-pacific","label":"Frontal proxies, separate-year sections and layered flow","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Data [5], Table 1 and STF [14]–[17]; Ridgway and Dunn (2007), section 3.4 [15].","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2024-12/010047303.pdf","summary":"The 103–88 W studied reach connects reported STF crossings sampled in 1994 and 1993. Frontal proxies are not velocity cores or simultaneous geometry. The 150 m temperature criterion does not define an axis depth; branch correspondence and whole-current dimensions remain unresolved. Layered gyre flow cannot be identified universally by the STF."},"source_sha256":"391b88da4e6660d7ad6ca8d2055333d26dca34b89fac4713720cff3a8112c189"}],"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_decision":{"candidate_ids":["south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-r